Dialogue: 0,0:00:02.00,0:00:07.00,Default,,0,0,0,,Downloaded from\NYTS.MX
Dialogue: 0,0:00:08.00,0:00:13.00,Default,,0,0,0,,Official YIFY movies site:\NYTS.MX
Dialogue: 0,0:00:11.31,0:00:16.23,Default,,0,0,0,,A Toho Production
Dialogue: 0,0:00:20.99,0:00:25.99,Default,,0,0,0,,Come on in.\NI’m glad you came.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:26.04,0:00:28.37,Default,,0,0,0,,How many years has it been?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:28.41,0:00:28.50,Default,,0,0,0,,- I’m sorry I didn’t keep in touch.\N- Forget it.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:28.50,0:00:31.33,Default,,0,0,0,,1926\N- I’m sorry I didn’t keep in touch.\N- Forget it.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:31.33,0:00:31.37,Default,,0,0,0,,1926
Dialogue: 0,0:00:31.37,0:00:33.83,Default,,0,0,0,,This is the first time\NI’ve visited you here.\N1926
Dialogue: 0,0:00:33.83,0:00:33.92,Default,,0,0,0,,- Really?\N- It’s a quiet town.\N1926
Dialogue: 0,0:00:33.92,0:00:35.29,Default,,0,0,0,,- Really?\N- It’s a quiet town.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:35.29,0:00:38.21,Default,,0,0,0,,Yoshino City\N- Really?\N- It’s a quiet town.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:38.21,0:00:39.92,Default,,0,0,0,,Yoshino City
Dialogue: 0,0:00:39.92,0:00:40.72,Default,,0,0,0,,You said you were going\Non a trip?\NYoshino City
Dialogue: 0,0:00:40.72,0:00:44.43,Default,,0,0,0,,You said you were going\Non a trip?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:44.72,0:00:46.60,Default,,0,0,0,,Have a seat.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:47.89,0:00:51.73,Default,,0,0,0,,I'll be away for a while.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:55.86,0:00:59.32,Default,,0,0,0,,Her name’s Tae.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:59.53,0:01:02.20,Default,,0,0,0,,She’s a distant relative.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:02.36,0:01:06.08,Default,,0,0,0,,She comes over to copy my manuscripts,\Nand helps the missus.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:06.28,0:01:09.16,Default,,0,0,0,,She’s studying to be a pharmacist.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:09.20,0:01:11.37,Default,,0,0,0,,My university major is pharmacology.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:11.87,0:01:16.63,Default,,0,0,0,,This is my friend Kindaichi.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:18.21,0:01:20.63,Default,,0,0,0,,He’s a detective.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:20.63,0:01:25.97,Default,,0,0,0,,He tends to disappear when\Nhe's working a difficult case.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:25.97,0:01:31.23,Default,,0,0,0,,I seem to remember such a character\Npopping up in your novels.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:31.23,0:01:34.23,Default,,0,0,0,,- I don’t recall.\N- Where are you going?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:34.23,0:01:36.40,Default,,0,0,0,,Maybe the US.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:36.73,0:01:39.57,Default,,0,0,0,,The US?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:39.82,0:01:44.07,Default,,0,0,0,,The US is quite advanced\Nin drugs for stress...
Dialogue: 0,0:01:44.28,0:01:47.16,Default,,0,0,0,,autism, and neurological conditions.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:47.28,0:01:49.74,Default,,0,0,0,,Are you really going?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:50.24,0:01:54.00,Default,,0,0,0,,People are the same all over.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:55.29,0:02:00.63,Default,,0,0,0,,Hey, Kindaichi is here!\NGet us some tea!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:00.88,0:02:02.97,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Just a second.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:02:08.10,0:02:11.06,Default,,0,0,0,,- Are you going by boat?\N- Yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:11.27,0:02:14.98,Default,,0,0,0,,- Have you gotten your passport?\N- Not yet.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:15.19,0:02:18.11,Default,,0,0,0,,- You’ll need a photograph.\N- I haven’t had one taken yet.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:18.31,0:02:23.99,Default,,0,0,0,,I know an old photography studio\Nthat's been in business since 1892.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:24.24,0:02:27.49,Default,,0,0,0,,I forget the name...
Dialogue: 0,0:02:27.66,0:02:31.12,Default,,0,0,0,,I haven’t been there in 7-8 years.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:33.66,0:02:37.00,Default,,0,0,0,,- He’s talking about the Honjo\NPhotography Studio. - That’s the one.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:37.67,0:02:40.96,Default,,0,0,0,,- Hello.\N- Thank you.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:41.17,0:02:43.92,Default,,0,0,0,,Kindaichi says he’s going to the US.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:44.13,0:02:45.76,Default,,0,0,0,,Wow, overseas!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:47.11,0:03:52.41,Default,,0,0,0,,Try to relax, you’re too stiff.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:52.58,0:03:56.20,Default,,0,0,0,,I can’t find it.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:56.41,0:03:58.12,Default,,0,0,0,,This house is too dark.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:58.16,0:04:02.93,Default,,0,0,0,,It has to be one of these. We'll have\Nto get a new one, but they’re all old.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:03.21,0:04:05.38,Default,,0,0,0,,- You should probably replace\Nall of them. - Hey, Mokutaro!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:05.59,0:04:07.80,Default,,0,0,0,,Shake a leg!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:08.42,0:04:12.18,Default,,0,0,0,,We used it for the US troops\Nduring the occupation.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:13.22,0:04:16.93,Default,,0,0,0,,- Where the heck is it?\N- You’re looking for the mountain vista?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:17.14,0:04:20.77,Default,,0,0,0,,We just used it the other day.\NWhy can’t you keep track of them?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:20.77,0:04:22.44,Default,,0,0,0,,Got it!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:23.69,0:04:27.07,Default,,0,0,0,,Damn, this one is for\Nchildren’s festivals.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:27.49,0:04:30.49,Default,,0,0,0,,Where in the world are\Nthose mountains?!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:30.49,0:04:32.70,Default,,0,0,0,,Just shoot my face.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:32.74,0:04:36.83,Default,,0,0,0,,We can’t very well have this\Nin the background.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:36.83,0:04:38.95,Default,,0,0,0,,It’s for a passport.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:40.04,0:04:42.88,Default,,0,0,0,,Then we need a white background!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:43.08,0:04:45.21,Default,,0,0,0,,You should have said so\Nfrom the start!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:54.76,0:04:58.39,Default,,0,0,0,,What are you doing, you boob?!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:58.60,0:05:03.02,Default,,0,0,0,,Are you all right?\NMy assistant is still new to his job.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:03.23,0:05:04.69,Default,,0,0,0,,I think I broke something!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:11.40,0:05:15.28,Default,,0,0,0,,Sorry, I thought you were out.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:15.49,0:05:19.37,Default,,0,0,0,,- What do you want?\N- The magnesium.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:19.58,0:05:22.62,Default,,0,0,0,,- It’s on the bottom shelf.\N- I found it. - Who’s the customer?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:22.83,0:05:25.58,Default,,0,0,0,,- He’s a bit unusual.\N- What?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:25.79,0:05:28.38,Default,,0,0,0,,He’s a private dick.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:29.46,0:05:31.63,Default,,0,0,0,,A flatfoot?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:31.80,0:05:36.01,Default,,0,0,0,,- Bombing raids were quite severe\Nin this area. - So they say.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:36.22,0:05:40.22,Default,,0,0,0,,I came back from Siberia in 1949.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:40.43,0:05:42.85,Default,,0,0,0,,The place was flattened.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:43.06,0:05:45.10,Default,,0,0,0,,I couldn’t even recognize it.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:45.31,0:05:49.57,Default,,0,0,0,,Japanese land forces had their\Nairfield right over there.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:49.82,0:05:52.11,Default,,0,0,0,,That would have been\Nthe enemy’s target.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:52.28,0:05:56.57,Default,,0,0,0,,- I can’t believe this building is still standing.\N- I suppose you’re right.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:57.74,0:06:01.29,Default,,0,0,0,,US troops are still stationed\Nin this town.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:01.50,0:06:04.42,Default,,0,0,0,,There’s a steep hill just yonder.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:04.58,0:06:07.04,Default,,0,0,0,,That’s Hospital Hill.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:07.29,0:06:08.88,Default,,0,0,0,,Hospital Hill?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:09.09,0:06:13.51,Default,,0,0,0,,It used to have a more ordinary name,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:13.72,0:06:19.14,Default,,0,0,0,,but a large hospital was built there\Nin the late 19th century.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:19.85,0:06:26.85,Default,,0,0,0,,People started to call it\N'Hospital Hill'.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:27.69,0:06:30.90,Default,,0,0,0,,It’s Hogen Hospital.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:31.11,0:06:33.36,Default,,0,0,0,,I didn’t notice the hospital.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:33.61,0:06:35.74,Default,,0,0,0,,Don’t move, I’m going to shoot.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:35.95,0:06:39.83,Default,,0,0,0,,Raise your head a little...\Nchin down.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:40.03,0:06:43.16,Default,,0,0,0,,Magnesium up...\NReady!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:46.21,0:06:58.39,Default,,0,0,0,,The House of Hanging
Dialogue: 0,0:06:58.93,0:07:02.64,Default,,0,0,0,,Produced by Kon Ichikawa
Dialogue: 0,0:07:05.68,0:07:09.69,Default,,0,0,0,,Based on a work by Seishi Yokomizo
Dialogue: 0,0:07:09.90,0:07:14.03,Default,,0,0,0,,Screenplay by\NShinya Hidaka and Tei Kurisu
Dialogue: 0,0:08:05.24,0:08:07.75,Default,,0,0,0,,Starring:
Dialogue: 0,0:08:08.29,0:08:12.63,Default,,0,0,0,,Yoshiko Sakuma
Dialogue: 0,0:08:12.84,0:08:15.88,Default,,0,0,0,,Masao Kusakari
Dialogue: 0,0:08:16.09,0:08:19.30,Default,,0,0,0,,Junko Sakurada
Dialogue: 0,0:08:26.27,0:08:30.77,Default,,0,0,0,,Takako Irie\NTakeshi Kato
Dialogue: 0,0:08:31.73,0:08:36.15,Default,,0,0,0,,Mitsuko Kusabue\NKayoko Shiraishi\NMiki Sanjo
Dialogue: 0,0:08:36.98,0:08:41.45,Default,,0,0,0,,Midori Hagio\NPeter\NKie Nakai
Dialogue: 0,0:08:43.07,0:08:47.66,Default,,0,0,0,,Hideji Otaki\NNobuto Okamoto\NEitaro Ozaka
Dialogue: 0,0:08:47.75,0:08:52.58,Default,,0,0,0,,Koji Shimizu, Akiji Kobayashi,\NFujio Tokita, Koreharu Hisatomi
Dialogue: 0,0:08:53.92,0:08:59.13,Default,,0,0,0,,Noboru Mitani, Sabu Kawahara,\NYutaka Hayashi, Shingo Yamamoto,\NBunji Hayata
Dialogue: 0,0:08:59.47,0:09:02.47,Default,,0,0,0,,Teruhiko Aoi
Dialogue: 0,0:09:02.55,0:09:06.22,Default,,0,0,0,,Special appearances by\NSeishi Yokomizo and Norihei Miki
Dialogue: 0,0:09:06.97,0:09:11.69,Default,,0,0,0,,Koji Ishizaka as Kosuke Kindaichi
Dialogue: 0,0:09:11.85,0:09:17.36,Default,,0,0,0,,Directed by Kon Ichikawa
Dialogue: 0,0:09:17.94,0:09:21.53,Default,,0,0,0,,You’re going to be killed?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:24.11,0:09:26.78,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:29.66,0:09:34.46,Default,,0,0,0,,I ran an errand the other day.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:34.67,0:09:38.67,Default,,0,0,0,,I went to see a burned-out building.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:38.88,0:09:45.97,Default,,0,0,0,,Just as I was about to enter through\Nthe inward-opening door,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:46.22,0:09:50.22,Default,,0,0,0,,these huge wind chimes\Nplopped right down on me!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:50.43,0:09:54.65,Default,,0,0,0,,Wind chimes? You mean those things that tinkle\Nwhen the wind blows in the summer.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:54.81,0:09:58.27,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes! It still hurts.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:59.73,0:10:03.65,Default,,0,0,0,,It was only because I stopped in\Nthe doorway...
Dialogue: 0,0:10:03.86,0:10:08.62,Default,,0,0,0,,when the superintendent\Ncalled out my name...
Dialogue: 0,0:10:09.20,0:10:15.21,Default,,0,0,0,,that the wind chimes\Nonly grazed my shoulder.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:15.42,0:10:17.75,Default,,0,0,0,,If I'd been hit directly,\NI’d have been a goner.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:19.25,0:10:21.51,Default,,0,0,0,,Do you think it was a trap?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:23.05,0:10:25.68,Default,,0,0,0,,Why would someone want to kill you?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:26.14,0:10:30.10,Default,,0,0,0,,I don’t know.\NThat’s why I want you to check it out.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:30.18,0:10:33.98,Default,,0,0,0,,- PIs provide such services,\Ndon't they? - Of course.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:34.39,0:10:37.02,Default,,0,0,0,,I’d be happy to pay.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:39.52,0:10:43.90,Default,,0,0,0,,But you mustn’t tell anyone\Nabout this.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:49.95,0:10:53.20,Default,,0,0,0,,What did my father want with you?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:53.33,0:10:54.66,Default,,0,0,0,,We were just talking.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:55.50,0:10:57.96,Default,,0,0,0,,You have a lot of old photos.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:58.38,0:11:00.38,Default,,0,0,0,,Did you take them all yourself?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:00.92,0:11:04.92,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes, me and two other generations\Nof photographers.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:05.76,0:11:10.89,Default,,0,0,0,,The Meiji, Taisho, and Showa periods.\NIt’s like a museum exhibit.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:11.10,0:11:13.72,Default,,0,0,0,,The family has always prided itself\Nin being well organized.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:14.10,0:11:17.27,Default,,0,0,0,,Everything is organized and preserved,\Nfrom the plates to the film.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:17.39,0:11:21.11,Default,,0,0,0,,I see. When will my photo be ready?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:21.32,0:11:23.19,Default,,0,0,0,,In three days.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:23.73,0:11:25.61,Default,,0,0,0,,I'll see you then.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:38.17,0:11:40.63,Default,,0,0,0,,Detective, did you forget something?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:53.72,0:11:55.18,Default,,0,0,0,,Can I help you?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:58.14,0:12:00.10,Default,,0,0,0,,I want a photo taken.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:01.27,0:12:03.98,Default,,0,0,0,,- Please, come in.\N- I want it on location.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:04.94,0:12:06.32,Default,,0,0,0,,Where?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:07.32,0:12:09.32,Default,,0,0,0,,- I can’t say.\N- Why not?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:09.53,0:12:10.82,Default,,0,0,0,,It’s not far.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:11.12,0:12:14.33,Default,,0,0,0,,We need to know the location\Nof the shoot.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:14.54,0:12:17.83,Default,,0,0,0,,Tonight at 9:00.\NI'll send someone to pick you up.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:18.29,0:12:20.54,Default,,0,0,0,,All right.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:21.38,0:12:26.13,Default,,0,0,0,,What kind of a photo do you need?\NWe need to make preparations.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:26.21,0:12:27.42,Default,,0,0,0,,A wedding photo.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:27.67,0:12:30.72,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, congratulations.\NYours?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:30.93,0:12:34.18,Default,,0,0,0,,No, my sister’s.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:35.01,0:12:37.64,Default,,0,0,0,,Here’s ¥2,000.\NI hope it’s enough.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:37.85,0:12:40.35,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, you'll be paying in advance?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:40.60,0:12:44.86,Default,,0,0,0,,- When will the photo be ready?\N- If you’re in a hurry, two days.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:44.94,0:12:48.65,Default,,0,0,0,,Someone will be by to pick them up.\NPlease leave them out.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:48.86,0:12:50.20,Default,,0,0,0,,Thank you.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:53.07,0:12:56.66,Default,,0,0,0,,She didn’t leave her name.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:56.74,0:12:59.41,Default,,0,0,0,,She sure was a honey.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:08.88,0:13:12.43,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Honjo Photography Studio{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:13:12.64,0:13:14.60,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Who’s there?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:13:18.47,0:13:22.02,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, the wedding shoot?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:23.10,0:13:26.19,Default,,0,0,0,,Thank you for coming.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:37.58,0:13:42.71,Default,,0,0,0,,Isn’t this the Hogens’ house?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:43.83,0:13:49.00,Default,,0,0,0,,It is.\NWe’re relatives.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:49.30,0:13:52.09,Default,,0,0,0,,- I thought this house was abandoned.\N- Shaddap!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:09.82,0:14:14.20,Default,,0,0,0,,Set up your equipment here\Nand wait.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:39.47,0:14:41.35,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}OK, we’re ready!{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:14:41.52,0:14:43.60,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Open the door and come in!{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:15:07.96,0:15:10.25,Default,,0,0,0,,Hurry up and take the photo already!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:16.43,0:15:20.51,Default,,0,0,0,,That’s a strange place to hang wind chimes.\NThe photo will be better without them.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:20.76,0:15:24.81,Default,,0,0,0,,Don’t touch them.\NIt’s a family tradition.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:24.89,0:15:26.64,Default,,0,0,0,,If you say so.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:36.86,0:15:39.32,Default,,0,0,0,,The bride’s lapels are crooked...
Dialogue: 0,0:15:39.49,0:15:40.66,Default,,0,0,0,,Stay back!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:41.20,0:15:42.54,Default,,0,0,0,,I'll do it.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:50.13,0:15:51.88,Default,,0,0,0,,OK, perfect.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:16.44,0:16:18.78,Default,,0,0,0,,Good morning, are they done?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:21.37,0:16:24.12,Default,,0,0,0,,Let me have a look.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:30.75,0:16:33.46,Default,,0,0,0,,So let me get this straight, Dad...
Dialogue: 0,0:16:33.63,0:16:37.67,Default,,0,0,0,,She’s a ringer for a girl at\NHogen Hospital named Yukari?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:40.05,0:16:41.76,Default,,0,0,0,,I don’t know the groom.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:42.18,0:16:43.97,Default,,0,0,0,,He was pushy.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:44.10,0:16:45.64,Default,,0,0,0,,Soap.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:46.68,0:16:48.93,Default,,0,0,0,,Cigarettes.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:49.52,0:16:52.65,Default,,0,0,0,,You have stockings?\NYes, if you have them.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:54.40,0:16:58.36,Default,,0,0,0,,Not again? You shouldn’t traffic\Nin the US troops’ supplies.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:58.57,0:17:01.24,Default,,0,0,0,,I didn’t ask for your opinion.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:02.11,0:17:05.16,Default,,0,0,0,,I know.\NIf you don’t care, I don’t care.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:06.99,0:17:10.04,Default,,0,0,0,,- Good evening.\N- Good evening.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:10.21,0:17:14.08,Default,,0,0,0,,- Detective, I’m sorry, but your photos aren’t\Nready yet. - Really? Is the owner here?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:14.29,0:17:16.55,Default,,0,0,0,,There’s something I wanted to\Nspeak with him about.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:17.17,0:17:18.92,Default,,0,0,0,,Could you take a look at this for me?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:18.96,0:17:21.43,Default,,0,0,0,,- The owner?\N- Please.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:25.14,0:17:27.81,Default,,0,0,0,,It’s a wedding photo.\NWhat about it?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:28.06,0:17:32.52,Default,,0,0,0,,The location is... strange.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:33.65,0:17:37.15,Default,,0,0,0,,Not really, there’s a gold folding screen\Nin the background.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:37.23,0:17:41.15,Default,,0,0,0,,It’s the house.\NI thought it was abandoned…
Dialogue: 0,0:17:41.36,0:17:44.37,Default,,0,0,0,,- But it isn’t!\N- No, actually it is.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:45.07,0:17:49.45,Default,,0,0,0,,But my dad hollered at me to\Ngo check it out this morning.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:49.66,0:17:53.29,Default,,0,0,0,,I went and found the screen,\Nthe rug, the chair… all gone.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:53.37,0:17:58.42,Default,,0,0,0,,Young sir, the girl who made the reservation\Nfor the photo shoot was the bride.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:58.55,0:17:59.96,Default,,0,0,0,,Shut your trap.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:00.88,0:18:04.18,Default,,0,0,0,,There’s something hanging between\Nthe bride and the groom.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:04.39,0:18:07.60,Default,,0,0,0,,- They’re wind chimes.\N- Wind chimes?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:09.81,0:18:16.65,Default,,0,0,0,,The one unusual thing is that the\Nbride’s eyes look like she’s dreaming.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:16.90,0:18:19.02,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes, they do.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:19.28,0:18:22.19,Default,,0,0,0,,It’s strange. I thought the whole thing\Nwas weird last night.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:22.19,0:18:24.74,Default,,0,0,0,,- Was she alive?\N- That’s a lurid question.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:24.74,0:18:27.58,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes, she was breathing.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:27.62,0:18:30.16,Default,,0,0,0,,Detective, I was just thinking...
Dialogue: 0,0:18:30.20,0:18:33.62,Default,,0,0,0,,Maybe he drugged the girl because\Nshe didn’t want to get married,
Dialogue: 0,0:18:33.66,0:18:36.58,Default,,0,0,0,,and then held the ceremony.\NI should have gone along.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:36.79,0:18:38.38,Default,,0,0,0,,Shut up, already.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:38.63,0:18:44.47,Default,,0,0,0,,My dad said the bride may be of\Nthe family that owned Hogen Hospital.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:44.72,0:18:47.05,Default,,0,0,0,,That would seem even stranger to me,
Dialogue: 0,0:18:47.26,0:18:51.68,Default,,0,0,0,,the daughter of a prominent family holding\Nher wedding in a house with such a sordid past.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:51.72,0:18:53.02,Default,,0,0,0,,Sordid, you say?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:54.23,0:18:59.57,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes, that house is called\Nthe House of Hanging.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:00.02,0:19:02.15,Default,,0,0,0,,Why?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:02.19,0:19:09.20,Default,,0,0,0,,A woman was found hanged in the house\Na year after the War ended.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:15.29,0:19:17.79,Default,,0,0,0,,Hello.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:18.00,0:19:19.75,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes, that’s right.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:20.38,0:19:21.92,Default,,0,0,0,,What?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:24.17,0:19:26.84,Default,,0,0,0,,Hello? Hello?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:29.26,0:19:31.39,Default,,0,0,0,,- She hung up.\N- Who was it?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:32.14,0:19:33.52,Default,,0,0,0,,It sounded like a young woman.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:33.64,0:19:36.06,Default,,0,0,0,,She wanted to book another photo session\Ntonight in that same house.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:36.14,0:19:39.40,Default,,0,0,0,,- Was it the same girl as last night?\N- Yes, I’m sure it was her voice!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:39.61,0:19:42.15,Default,,0,0,0,,- What did she want you to shoot?\N- The wind chimes.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:16.48,0:20:19.98,Default,,0,0,0,,No one’s here.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:20.15,0:20:22.15,Default,,0,0,0,,Look here.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:29.20,0:20:30.91,Default,,0,0,0,,I don’t see any wind chimes.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:39.83,0:20:41.50,Default,,0,0,0,,It’s a severed head!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:52.60,0:20:53.85,Default,,0,0,0,,It’s the killer!
Dialogue: 0,0:22:41.08,0:22:44.33,Default,,0,0,0,,Aunt Yayoi, I’ve been expecting you.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:45.96,0:22:49.84,Default,,0,0,0,,You came by rickshaw again?\NI sent a car to pick you up.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:50.13,0:22:53.88,Default,,0,0,0,,I prefer Sannosuke’s rickshaw.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:54.76,0:23:02.18,Default,,0,0,0,,This is the first time you’ve been here\Nsince the house was bombed out.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:03.39,0:23:08.27,Default,,0,0,0,,I just telephoned.\NI’m Detective Bando.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:08.61,0:23:12.82,Default,,0,0,0,,I’m sorry for the inconvenience.\NPlease come this way.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:13.82,0:23:16.32,Default,,0,0,0,,Don’t worry about taking off\Nyour shoes.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:18.41,0:23:23.70,Default,,0,0,0,,The incident was discovered late last night.\NWe just finished surveying the crime scene.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:23.91,0:23:28.83,Default,,0,0,0,,I’m afraid this is an unusual crime\Nwith few clues.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:29.04,0:23:31.88,Default,,0,0,0,,It was quite shocking.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:32.09,0:23:33.51,Default,,0,0,0,,She's here.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:34.92,0:23:38.09,Default,,0,0,0,,This is the lead investigator.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:38.80,0:23:41.31,Default,,0,0,0,,Todoroki of the prefectural police.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:41.81,0:23:43.56,Default,,0,0,0,,I’m Yayoi Hogen.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:43.97,0:23:49.31,Default,,0,0,0,,These three discovered the scene.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:52.11,0:23:56.15,Default,,0,0,0,,Yayoi, it’s been a long time.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:59.57,0:24:04.58,Default,,0,0,0,,This is my son, Naokichi,\Nand my apprentice, Mokutaro.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:05.41,0:24:09.38,Default,,0,0,0,,This man says he’s a private investigator.\NIsn’t that right?
Dialogue: 0,0:24:09.63,0:24:10.92,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:11.00,0:24:15.84,Default,,0,0,0,,He’s apparently being employed by\Nthe photographer’s father.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:16.01,0:24:17.84,Default,,0,0,0,,- Isn’t that right?\N- Yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:18.01,0:24:22.56,Default,,0,0,0,,This fellow just gave us a broad\Noverview of the incident.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:23.18,0:24:24.85,Default,,0,0,0,,Is this your son?
Dialogue: 0,0:24:25.02,0:24:26.27,Default,,0,0,0,,I’m not her son.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:26.52,0:24:29.44,Default,,0,0,0,,My name is Shigeru Igarashi.\NThat woman is my mother.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:29.60,0:24:32.82,Default,,0,0,0,,However, she just identified herself\Nas Mitsue Tanabe.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:32.94,0:24:35.32,Default,,0,0,0,,That’s right.\NIgarashi is my father’s name.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:35.48,0:24:37.82,Default,,0,0,0,,My mother uses her maiden name.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:37.99,0:24:41.49,Default,,0,0,0,,I used to go by the surname of Tanabe,\Nbut I changed it for matters of inheritance.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:41.49,0:24:43.70,Default,,0,0,0,,But you’re all living together, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:24:43.87,0:24:47.41,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes, the two families are\Nconnected by marriage.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:47.62,0:24:51.54,Default,,0,0,0,,- Yayoi is my aunt.\N- I understand now.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:51.58,0:24:53.96,Default,,0,0,0,,- Do you really?\N- Shaddap!
Dialogue: 0,0:24:54.17,0:24:56.67,Default,,0,0,0,,Don’t embarrass me when\NI’m on a case!
Dialogue: 0,0:24:56.84,0:25:01.05,Default,,0,0,0,,Has last night’s suspect calmed down?\NGo talk to him.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:01.22,0:25:03.51,Default,,0,0,0,,He might have something useful to say.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:07.22,0:25:10.73,Default,,0,0,0,,I believe you were told on the phone...
Dialogue: 0,0:25:11.06,0:25:15.36,Default,,0,0,0,,that there’s something we want to\Ncheck with you about.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:16.15,0:25:20.03,Default,,0,0,0,,But you can see the crime scene\Nfirst if you’d like.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:20.15,0:25:21.70,Default,,0,0,0,,Yayoi, there’s no reason for you\Nto see that!
Dialogue: 0,0:25:22.03,0:25:25.53,Default,,0,0,0,,I caught a glimpse of it and\NI almost fainted.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:25.95,0:25:27.87,Default,,0,0,0,,No, I’d like to see it.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:28.00,0:25:31.67,Default,,0,0,0,,It’s my home,\Nso I bear some responsibility here.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:38.26,0:25:41.59,Default,,0,0,0,,Have you found the body that\Nbelongs to the head?
Dialogue: 0,0:25:41.88,0:25:44.80,Default,,0,0,0,,No. We've combed the house\Nand the grounds.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:45.01,0:25:48.35,Default,,0,0,0,,The police think that the murder was\Ncommitted somewhere else.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:49.18,0:25:50.89,Default,,0,0,0,,But, I…
Dialogue: 0,0:25:51.64,0:25:54.86,Default,,0,0,0,,- Oh, how dreadful!\N- Oh, Yayoi!
Dialogue: 0,0:25:55.94,0:26:00.57,Default,,0,0,0,,I wanted you to look at this photograph.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:01.15,0:26:04.07,Default,,0,0,0,,The victim was almost certainly\Nthe groom,
Dialogue: 0,0:26:04.70,0:26:07.54,Default,,0,0,0,,but is the bride your daughter?
Dialogue: 0,0:26:07.79,0:26:11.04,Default,,0,0,0,,More to the point,\Nshe's been identified as Yukari Hogen.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:11.08,0:26:13.79,Default,,0,0,0,,- Can you confirm this?\N- It’s her, isn’t it?
Dialogue: 0,0:26:14.00,0:26:15.92,Default,,0,0,0,,I told him it was.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:16.75,0:26:21.09,Default,,0,0,0,,The woman’s makeup is thick,\Nso it’s hard to say for sure,
Dialogue: 0,0:26:21.30,0:26:25.26,Default,,0,0,0,,but she clearly looks like my daughter.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:25.80,0:26:29.77,Default,,0,0,0,,"Looks like her"?! Are you asserting\Nthat is in fact not your daughter?!
Dialogue: 0,0:26:30.10,0:26:32.06,Default,,0,0,0,,- It’s Yukari, I tell you!\N- No, it’s not.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:32.98,0:26:35.06,Default,,0,0,0,,I know my own daughter.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:35.40,0:26:39.28,Default,,0,0,0,,Anyway, she’s at my house now.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:40.11,0:26:43.07,Default,,0,0,0,,You said some strange things\Non the telephone,
Dialogue: 0,0:26:43.61,0:26:47.32,Default,,0,0,0,,so I thought it would be best\Nto bring her here.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:47.78,0:26:50.20,Default,,0,0,0,,She should be along shortly.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:50.74,0:26:53.33,Default,,0,0,0,,About the severed head...
Dialogue: 0,0:26:53.37,0:26:58.96,Default,,0,0,0,,Murderers usually try to conceal their\Nvictim’s identity, or hide the body altogether.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:58.96,0:27:02.84,Default,,0,0,0,,Why would anyone go to the trouble\Nof displaying the head like that?
Dialogue: 0,0:27:03.05,0:27:05.51,Default,,0,0,0,,You simpleton, it’s obvious!
Dialogue: 0,0:27:05.76,0:27:10.64,Default,,0,0,0,,To trip up the investigation, of course.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:12.77,0:27:14.44,Default,,0,0,0,,Yukari!
Dialogue: 0,0:27:32.95,0:27:36.29,Default,,0,0,0,,My daughter, Yukari.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:43.42,0:27:46.22,Default,,0,0,0,,This photo looks just like her.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:46.72,0:27:51.68,Default,,0,0,0,,So, who in the world is this bride?!
Dialogue: 0,0:27:52.10,0:27:54.81,Default,,0,0,0,,- Detective Todoroki!\N- What is it?
Dialogue: 0,0:27:55.23,0:27:58.77,Default,,0,0,0,,We learned the identities of\Nthe victim and the bride.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:59.02,0:28:01.27,Default,,0,0,0,,- What?\N- Our suspect confirmed it!
Dialogue: 0,0:28:06.90,0:28:09.70,Default,,0,0,0,,Hey, who is it?
Dialogue: 0,0:28:10.99,0:28:12.58,Default,,0,0,0,,Answer me!
Dialogue: 0,0:28:13.74,0:28:17.58,Default,,0,0,0,,It’s Toshio and Koyuki Yamauchi.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:17.79,0:28:22.63,Default,,0,0,0,,He and they were in a group called\N{\i1}The Angry Pirates{\i0}.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:22.67,0:28:25.17,Default,,0,0,0,,Who are 'The Angry Pirates'?
Dialogue: 0,0:28:25.38,0:28:31.68,Default,,0,0,0,,A jazz band that plays exclusively\Nat US military bases in Japan.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:31.76,0:28:33.51,Default,,0,0,0,,Officer, I haven’t killed anyone.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:33.56,0:28:35.52,Default,,0,0,0,,Then why didn’t you speak out\Nbefore now?
Dialogue: 0,0:28:35.60,0:28:37.77,Default,,0,0,0,,I was scared and upset.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:37.98,0:28:39.81,Default,,0,0,0,,The two people in the photo were\Nboth named Yamauchi.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:40.02,0:28:42.61,Default,,0,0,0,,- They were brother and sister.\N- Then why would they be getting married?!
Dialogue: 0,0:28:42.69,0:28:44.86,Default,,0,0,0,,They weren’t blood relations.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:46.94,0:28:51.70,Default,,0,0,0,,What were you doing here last night?
Dialogue: 0,0:28:52.32,0:28:55.41,Default,,0,0,0,,They both took a day off work yesterday,\Nso I came to see what they were doing.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:55.62,0:28:57.37,Default,,0,0,0,,How did you know they’d be here?
Dialogue: 0,0:28:57.46,0:28:59.79,Default,,0,0,0,,Because of the wedding photo.
Dialogue: 0,0:29:00.12,0:29:05.05,Default,,0,0,0,,The night before last, the couple was\Nsecretly married in this very house,
Dialogue: 0,0:29:05.09,0:29:08.76,Default,,0,0,0,,and Yoshizawa was the only\Nperson who helped.
Dialogue: 0,0:29:08.97,0:29:11.22,Default,,0,0,0,,- Am I right?!\N- Yes...
Dialogue: 0,0:29:11.26,0:29:13.72,Default,,0,0,0,,I borrowed the folding screens\Nand the rug.
Dialogue: 0,0:29:13.80,0:29:16.31,Default,,0,0,0,,Then, I took the line from\Na power pole for electricity.
Dialogue: 0,0:29:16.39,0:29:18.85,Default,,0,0,0,,It was a lot of work.
Dialogue: 0,0:29:18.93,0:29:21.69,Default,,0,0,0,,I came to see if they were still here,
Dialogue: 0,0:29:21.85,0:29:26.69,Default,,0,0,0,,and I saw Toshio’s severed head dangling\Nfrom the ceiling! I was terrified.
Dialogue: 0,0:29:26.90,0:29:31.20,Default,,0,0,0,,Then those people came,\Nand I panicked and ran.
Dialogue: 0,0:29:31.45,0:29:34.12,Default,,0,0,0,,I’m not the killer!\NYou must believe me!
Dialogue: 0,0:29:34.41,0:29:36.74,Default,,0,0,0,,We'll find that out soon enough.
Dialogue: 0,0:29:36.87,0:29:39.21,Default,,0,0,0,,Where are you all staying?
Dialogue: 0,0:29:39.41,0:29:42.08,Default,,0,0,0,,- We don’t all live together.\N- What about the two Yamauchis?!
Dialogue: 0,0:29:42.29,0:29:46.38,Default,,0,0,0,,They rented a garage outside of town.
Dialogue: 0,0:29:59.06,0:30:00.52,Default,,0,0,0,,What is this place?
Dialogue: 0,0:30:01.19,0:30:03.40,Default,,0,0,0,,It was flattened in the war.
Dialogue: 0,0:30:03.65,0:30:06.36,Default,,0,0,0,,- Is this the garage?\N- Yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:30:43.56,0:30:45.48,Default,,0,0,0,,Musical instruments...
Dialogue: 0,0:30:49.73,0:30:51.57,Default,,0,0,0,,Did you find Koyuki?
Dialogue: 0,0:30:51.69,0:30:53.95,Default,,0,0,0,,No. Open the door.
Dialogue: 0,0:30:54.16,0:30:56.66,Default,,0,0,0,,- The door?\N- Yes, open it.
Dialogue: 0,0:31:18.35,0:31:20.68,Default,,0,0,0,,It’s blood!
Dialogue: 0,0:31:33.11,0:31:37.87,Default,,0,0,0,,Sir, is that…
Dialogue: 0,0:31:41.20,0:31:45.87,Default,,0,0,0,,Koyuki’s body is under that tarp.\NPull off the tarp.
Dialogue: 0,0:31:46.62,0:31:51.05,Default,,0,0,0,,- You mean… by myself?\N- Yes, do it.
Dialogue: 0,0:32:03.64,0:32:06.60,Default,,0,0,0,,This must be where the head\Nwas cut off.
Dialogue: 0,0:32:07.98,0:32:11.48,Default,,0,0,0,,OK, I figured it out.\NIt was here.
Dialogue: 0,0:32:12.15,0:32:13.36,Default,,0,0,0,,Sir!
Dialogue: 0,0:32:13.40,0:32:15.03,Default,,0,0,0,,- What?\N- Look!
Dialogue: 0,0:32:17.82,0:32:22.41,Default,,0,0,0,,A bloody footprint.\NIt must be…
Dialogue: 0,0:32:22.66,0:32:24.58,Default,,0,0,0,,the murderer’s footprint!
Dialogue: 0,0:32:24.83,0:32:27.41,Default,,0,0,0,,They look like army boots.
Dialogue: 0,0:32:30.46,0:32:32.75,Default,,0,0,0,,Do you know something about this?
Dialogue: 0,0:32:32.96,0:32:34.13,Default,,0,0,0,,Well?
Dialogue: 0,0:32:35.84,0:32:40.39,Default,,0,0,0,,There was another man that came\Nlooking for Toshio and Koyuki,
Dialogue: 0,0:32:40.43,0:32:43.35,Default,,0,0,0,,before I went to the empty house\Non Hospital Hill.
Dialogue: 0,0:32:43.39,0:32:47.02,Default,,0,0,0,,- Who?\N- The drummer, Sagawa.
Dialogue: 0,0:32:51.44,0:32:55.48,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Severed Head Wind Chime\NMurder Investigation Site{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:32:57.15,0:32:58.78,Default,,0,0,0,,What?
Dialogue: 0,0:33:02.28,0:33:04.54,Default,,0,0,0,,It’s an {\i1}Angry Pirates{\i0} concert.
Dialogue: 0,0:33:07.62,0:33:09.75,Default,,0,0,0,,Koyuki was the singer.
Dialogue: 0,0:33:11.67,0:33:15.42,Default,,0,0,0,,She’s a dead ringer for Yukari Hogen.
Dialogue: 0,0:33:17.63,0:33:21.72,Default,,0,0,0,,Sagawa. I understand you were\Nfighting with Toshio during...
Dialogue: 0,0:33:21.93,0:33:23.51,Default,,0,0,0,,the performance the day\Nbefore yesterday.
Dialogue: 0,0:33:23.68,0:33:26.64,Default,,0,0,0,,- Yes.\N- And Toshio punched you in the eye.
Dialogue: 0,0:33:28.64,0:33:30.52,Default,,0,0,0,,What was the fight about?
Dialogue: 0,0:33:30.85,0:33:34.02,Default,,0,0,0,,Toshio said he was going to\Nmarry Koyuki.
Dialogue: 0,0:33:34.77,0:33:37.53,Default,,0,0,0,,He whisked her off in the middle\Nof the performance.
Dialogue: 0,0:33:37.57,0:33:40.36,Default,,0,0,0,,And you were sweet on her?
Dialogue: 0,0:33:44.07,0:33:48.00,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes. I’m sure she loved him\Nas a brother,
Dialogue: 0,0:33:48.16,0:33:51.04,Default,,0,0,0,,but I never imagined she’d\Nmarry the guy.
Dialogue: 0,0:33:51.42,0:33:55.34,Default,,0,0,0,,So you attacked them at the garage\Nin a jealous fit?
Dialogue: 0,0:33:55.67,0:33:59.47,Default,,0,0,0,,Of course I was angry when I went there!\NBut I had no intention of killing them!
Dialogue: 0,0:33:59.67,0:34:01.38,Default,,0,0,0,,Ask the other band members!
Dialogue: 0,0:34:02.26,0:34:04.22,Default,,0,0,0,,I was worried about them!
Dialogue: 0,0:34:05.26,0:34:07.97,Default,,0,0,0,,But they were already gone\Nwhen I arrived.
Dialogue: 0,0:34:08.02,0:34:11.64,Default,,0,0,0,,- There was blood all over the place,\Nso I split. - Liar!
Dialogue: 0,0:34:12.06,0:34:16.27,Default,,0,0,0,,You’re hiding Koyuki.\NWhere is she?
Dialogue: 0,0:34:16.44,0:34:19.24,Default,,0,0,0,,I wish I knew.
Dialogue: 0,0:34:20.07,0:34:21.82,Default,,0,0,0,,- Detective!\N- What?
Dialogue: 0,0:34:23.74,0:34:25.62,Default,,0,0,0,,What is it?
Dialogue: 0,0:34:26.45,0:34:28.41,Default,,0,0,0,,The results are back from the lab.
Dialogue: 0,0:34:28.66,0:34:31.71,Default,,0,0,0,,I discovered that it was indeed blood\Non the soles of Sagawa’s shoes.
Dialogue: 0,0:34:31.71,0:34:33.21,Default,,0,0,0,,A positive luminal test?
Dialogue: 0,0:34:33.46,0:34:38.67,Default,,0,0,0,,It’s blood. And according to the ME’s\Nreport on the head…
Dialogue: 0,0:34:38.67,0:34:40.51,Default,,0,0,0,,What’s this?
Dialogue: 0,0:34:40.71,0:34:44.80,Default,,0,0,0,,It was severed around two hours\Nafter death.
Dialogue: 0,0:34:44.84,0:34:50.43,Default,,0,0,0,,So Toshio must have died between\N8:00-10:00pm the day before yesterday.
Dialogue: 0,0:34:50.64,0:34:52.06,Default,,0,0,0,,10:00pm?
Dialogue: 0,0:34:55.52,0:34:59.32,Default,,0,0,0,,That coincides with the time that\NSagawa was at the garage.
Dialogue: 0,0:35:00.57,0:35:04.53,Default,,0,0,0,,I figured it out!
Dialogue: 0,0:35:04.78,0:35:08.87,Default,,0,0,0,,Our killers are Sagawa and Koyuki!\NUse your head.
Dialogue: 0,0:35:09.83,0:35:12.16,Default,,0,0,0,,Both had motive...
Dialogue: 0,0:35:12.58,0:35:15.88,Default,,0,0,0,,Koyuki was being forced\Nto marry Toshio,
Dialogue: 0,0:35:16.33,0:35:20.30,Default,,0,0,0,,and Sagawa was the rival\Nfor her affections.
Dialogue: 0,0:35:20.67,0:35:24.55,Default,,0,0,0,,This kind of sloppy crime is the\Nall-too-common upshot of love triangles.
Dialogue: 0,0:35:24.55,0:35:27.72,Default,,0,0,0,,We already have Sagawa.\NPut out an APB on Koyuki.
Dialogue: 0,0:35:29.10,0:35:30.81,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, Mr. Kindaichi.
Dialogue: 0,0:35:31.77,0:35:35.94,Default,,0,0,0,,- What is it?\N- I’d like to see Officer Kano.
Dialogue: 0,0:35:38.48,0:35:40.65,Default,,0,0,0,,Kano - oh, the former detective?
Dialogue: 0,0:35:40.98,0:35:43.40,Default,,0,0,0,,He’s in the Crime Prevention Division now.
Dialogue: 0,0:35:43.49,0:35:44.86,Default,,0,0,0,,What do you want?!
Dialogue: 0,0:35:45.36,0:35:49.41,Default,,0,0,0,,He was the officer in charge when\Nthe woman hanged herself.
Dialogue: 0,0:35:49.62,0:35:51.91,Default,,0,0,0,,I just wanted to go over\Na few details.
Dialogue: 0,0:35:52.16,0:35:54.71,Default,,0,0,0,,Details related to this investigation?
Dialogue: 0,0:35:54.75,0:35:57.88,Default,,0,0,0,,I’m not sure yet. Goodbye.
Dialogue: 0,0:35:59.88,0:36:05.26,Default,,0,0,0,,I’ve seen that fella somewhere before.\NDo you know him?
Dialogue: 0,0:36:05.38,0:36:07.51,Default,,0,0,0,,Never met him.
Dialogue: 0,0:36:09.68,0:36:11.26,Default,,0,0,0,,Not again!
Dialogue: 0,0:36:16.27,0:36:18.27,Default,,0,0,0,,They’re at it again.
Dialogue: 0,0:36:18.48,0:36:23.32,Default,,0,0,0,,I’ve asked the fire department to\Nput up signs banning campfires here,
Dialogue: 0,0:36:23.73,0:36:26.20,Default,,0,0,0,,but do they listen?
Dialogue: 0,0:36:26.40,0:36:32.45,Default,,0,0,0,,I know, you found me by checking\Nan old newspaper.
Dialogue: 0,0:36:32.66,0:36:36.21,Default,,0,0,0,,That was my last investigation\Nas a detective.
Dialogue: 0,0:36:36.71,0:36:40.42,Default,,0,0,0,,Mr. Kano,\Naccording to the newspaper,
Dialogue: 0,0:36:40.58,0:36:44.59,Default,,0,0,0,,the head was from a 33-year-old woman\Nnamed Fuyuko Yamauchi.
Dialogue: 0,0:36:44.63,0:36:47.68,Default,,0,0,0,,- That’s right.\N- What was the method of suicide?
Dialogue: 0,0:36:47.88,0:36:51.01,Default,,0,0,0,,The newspaper said the motive was under\Ninvestigation, but there were no further reports.
Dialogue: 0,0:36:51.05,0:36:53.89,Default,,0,0,0,,- We never found out.\N- There was no note? - Nope.
Dialogue: 0,0:36:54.72,0:36:57.43,Default,,0,0,0,,What kind of a person was she?
Dialogue: 0,0:36:57.48,0:37:03.69,Default,,0,0,0,,She had close ties to the abandoned\NHogen House.
Dialogue: 0,0:37:03.90,0:37:10.16,Default,,0,0,0,,I followed every lead in the case.
Dialogue: 0,0:37:11.87,0:37:17.87,Default,,0,0,0,,She was the mistress of the\Nhospital director, Tatsuya Hogen.
Dialogue: 0,0:37:18.08,0:37:23.17,Default,,0,0,0,,Tatsuya died in an air raid about\Na year before the incident.
Dialogue: 0,0:37:23.21,0:37:28.34,Default,,0,0,0,,- And Tatsuya’s wife was Yayoi?\N- Yes, legally.
Dialogue: 0,0:37:29.59,0:37:32.22,Default,,0,0,0,,Did Fuyuko have children?
Dialogue: 0,0:37:32.26,0:37:35.06,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes, a boy and a girl.
Dialogue: 0,0:37:35.47,0:37:40.19,Default,,0,0,0,,The boy was Toshio\Nand the girl was Koyuki.
Dialogue: 0,0:37:41.19,0:37:45.61,Default,,0,0,0,,I remember it like it was yesterday.
Dialogue: 0,0:37:45.82,0:37:49.45,Default,,0,0,0,,It was so cruel, so sad.
Dialogue: 0,0:37:52.07,0:38:00.08,Default,,0,0,0,,Her two children standing below\Nher dangling corpse.
Dialogue: 0,0:38:00.25,0:38:02.79,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}HOGEN{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:38:03.79,0:38:06.63,Default,,0,0,0,,That those two children were\NFuyuko’s children...
Dialogue: 0,0:38:08.17,0:38:11.05,Default,,0,0,0,,seems like a cruel trick of fate.
Dialogue: 0,0:38:11.38,0:38:14.35,Default,,0,0,0,,After the incident five years ago,
Dialogue: 0,0:38:14.47,0:38:19.06,Default,,0,0,0,,you took great pains to find her children.
Dialogue: 0,0:38:20.35,0:38:22.56,Default,,0,0,0,,You know what I think?
Dialogue: 0,0:38:23.15,0:38:27.65,Default,,0,0,0,,Those two planned to send us\Nthe photos of their wedding...
Dialogue: 0,0:38:27.82,0:38:30.03,Default,,0,0,0,,and of the severed head.
Dialogue: 0,0:38:30.61,0:38:35.37,Default,,0,0,0,,- Why?\N- Mother, they hate the Hogen family.
Dialogue: 0,0:38:39.91,0:38:41.33,Default,,0,0,0,,Nonsense.
Dialogue: 0,0:38:41.37,0:38:44.92,Default,,0,0,0,,They don’t hate us.\NIt’s completely absurd.
Dialogue: 0,0:38:45.96,0:38:51.38,Default,,0,0,0,,The day before she hanged herself,\NFuyuko visited the Hogens’ house.
Dialogue: 0,0:38:52.68,0:39:00.47,Default,,0,0,0,,Something surely transpired,\Nbut who can say what?
Dialogue: 0,0:39:00.72,0:39:03.85,Default,,0,0,0,,What was Fuyuko Yamauchi’s job?
Dialogue: 0,0:39:04.06,0:39:07.65,Default,,0,0,0,,She was the wife of\Na struggling painter.
Dialogue: 0,0:39:08.02,0:39:10.40,Default,,0,0,0,,Her husband had a child from\Na prior marriage.
Dialogue: 0,0:39:10.90,0:39:12.15,Default,,0,0,0,,That was Toshio.
Dialogue: 0,0:39:12.36,0:39:17.24,Default,,0,0,0,,He up and died,\Nand Fuyuko raised him.
Dialogue: 0,0:39:17.41,0:39:22.58,Default,,0,0,0,,She was waiting tables at a cafe\Nwhen she met Takuya.
Dialogue: 0,0:39:22.79,0:39:25.33,Default,,0,0,0,,They were Koyuki’s parents.
Dialogue: 0,0:39:25.37,0:39:28.13,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes. While working as a doctor,
Dialogue: 0,0:39:28.34,0:39:31.76,Default,,0,0,0,,Takuya gained a measure of fame\Nas a songwriter.
Dialogue: 0,0:39:32.34,0:39:34.18,Default,,0,0,0,,A composer?
Dialogue: 0,0:39:34.38,0:39:39.81,Default,,0,0,0,,Yayoi was a strong woman.\NShe had no time for the arts.
Dialogue: 0,0:39:40.01,0:39:45.35,Default,,0,0,0,,Still, even now she’s running\Nthe hospital quite competently.
Dialogue: 0,0:39:45.52,0:39:49.44,Default,,0,0,0,,Did Yayoi know about Fuyuko?
Dialogue: 0,0:39:50.02,0:39:52.03,Default,,0,0,0,,Apparently so.
Dialogue: 0,0:39:52.32,0:39:55.70,Default,,0,0,0,,Thank you for your time.
Dialogue: 0,0:39:55.91,0:40:02.50,Default,,0,0,0,,That’s OK, I’m just killing time\Nuntil I retire next year.
Dialogue: 0,0:40:02.75,0:40:08.92,Default,,0,0,0,,This is more of a hobby than\Nanything else.
Dialogue: 0,0:40:11.59,0:40:16.38,Default,,0,0,0,,Say, did something happen at\Nthe abandoned Hogen house?
Dialogue: 0,0:40:16.47,0:40:19.80,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes, there was a severed head\Nhanging there.
Dialogue: 0,0:40:20.51,0:40:23.39,Default,,0,0,0,,Yukari hasn’t been home in three days,
Dialogue: 0,0:40:23.43,0:40:27.44,Default,,0,0,0,,so I was surprised to see her\Nat the house today.
Dialogue: 0,0:40:28.27,0:40:30.31,Default,,0,0,0,,Where was she?
Dialogue: 0,0:40:30.61,0:40:33.82,Default,,0,0,0,,Yukari was in our lodge on Mount Hiei.
Dialogue: 0,0:40:34.53,0:40:40.12,Default,,0,0,0,,When the police summoned us, you left first\Nand she arrived home right after that.
Dialogue: 0,0:40:40.37,0:40:45.04,Default,,0,0,0,,Once she makes up her mind,\Nshe doesn’t think of anything but herself.
Dialogue: 0,0:40:45.25,0:40:47.92,Default,,0,0,0,,It’s rather selfish of her.
Dialogue: 0,0:40:48.12,0:40:51.92,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Madam.{\i0}\NIt’s the head of internal medicine.
Dialogue: 0,0:40:56.22,0:40:58.38,Default,,0,0,0,,Mother! Mother!
Dialogue: 0,0:40:58.93,0:41:02.85,Default,,0,0,0,,I think Aunt Yayoi knew that Yukari\Nwas at the lodge.
Dialogue: 0,0:41:03.22,0:41:04.81,Default,,0,0,0,,What are you talking about?
Dialogue: 0,0:41:05.02,0:41:07.52,Default,,0,0,0,,I think she doesn’t want me\Nto see Yukari.
Dialogue: 0,0:41:07.73,0:41:11.27,Default,,0,0,0,,Aunt Yayoi doesn’t want me as\Nthe heir to the Hogen estate,
Dialogue: 0,0:41:11.48,0:41:14.32,Default,,0,0,0,,which is why she doesn’t want\Nme to marry Yukari.
Dialogue: 0,0:41:27.00,0:41:28.83,Default,,0,0,0,,Mr. Kindaichi?
Dialogue: 0,0:41:33.13,0:41:35.96,Default,,0,0,0,,I’m a relative of the Hogens.
Dialogue: 0,0:41:36.17,0:41:40.05,Default,,0,0,0,,Yayoi would like to speak with you.
Dialogue: 0,0:41:51.27,0:41:53.77,Default,,0,0,0,,I wanted to speak with you.
Dialogue: 0,0:41:54.36,0:41:57.23,Default,,0,0,0,,We met this morning.
Dialogue: 0,0:41:57.44,0:42:00.53,Default,,0,0,0,,Ah, yes. The PI.
Dialogue: 0,0:42:02.95,0:42:08.20,Default,,0,0,0,,I want you to find Koyuki Yamauchi.
Dialogue: 0,0:42:10.08,0:42:19.17,Default,,0,0,0,,I believe that she’s still alive.
Dialogue: 0,0:42:20.93,0:42:27.97,Default,,0,0,0,,Toshio and Koyuki were tied\Nto the Hogen family.
Dialogue: 0,0:42:28.02,0:42:30.98,Default,,0,0,0,,I know about the House of Hanging.
Dialogue: 0,0:42:32.35,0:42:34.23,Default,,0,0,0,,I see.
Dialogue: 0,0:42:34.98,0:42:39.99,Default,,0,0,0,,Just thinking about it\Ngives me the chills.
Dialogue: 0,0:42:41.45,0:42:45.83,Default,,0,0,0,,Fuyuko visited me just before\Nshe died.
Dialogue: 0,0:42:46.33,0:42:51.46,Default,,0,0,0,,I was out.\NShe talked to Yukari.
Dialogue: 0,0:42:51.71,0:42:53.33,Default,,0,0,0,,Yukari?
Dialogue: 0,0:42:53.54,0:42:57.13,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}She was 17.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:42:57.59,0:42:59.63,Default,,0,0,0,,Get out of here!
Dialogue: 0,0:43:02.42,0:43:07.76,Default,,0,0,0,,Why are you staring at me like that?!\NSay something!
Dialogue: 0,0:43:08.35,0:43:13.35,Default,,0,0,0,,I’m sorry.\NI came to see Yayoi.
Dialogue: 0,0:43:13.56,0:43:15.73,Default,,0,0,0,,Absolutely not!
Dialogue: 0,0:43:15.77,0:43:19.40,Default,,0,0,0,,You’re a stranger to this family.
Dialogue: 0,0:43:19.44,0:43:21.82,Default,,0,0,0,,You show up at our house and say\Nyou’re my dead father’s mistress.
Dialogue: 0,0:43:21.86,0:43:25.70,Default,,0,0,0,,I’m his daughter,\Ndid you think I’d let you in?!
Dialogue: 0,0:43:27.41,0:43:33.16,Default,,0,0,0,,I never guessed that he had\Na woman on the side.
Dialogue: 0,0:43:34.12,0:43:38.04,Default,,0,0,0,,I know you’re angry...
Dialogue: 0,0:43:39.80,0:43:46.18,Default,,0,0,0,,but I’d like to talk with\Nyour mother.
Dialogue: 0,0:43:48.01,0:43:51.02,Default,,0,0,0,,I beg you...
Dialogue: 0,0:43:51.31,0:43:55.69,Default,,0,0,0,,Please...\NLet me see her!
Dialogue: 0,0:43:56.06,0:43:59.36,Default,,0,0,0,,You’re broke.\NYou want money, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:43:59.57,0:44:01.73,Default,,0,0,0,,- No!\N- Liar! - No.
Dialogue: 0,0:44:01.98,0:44:05.65,Default,,0,0,0,,Beggar!\NYou’re worse than a beggar.
Dialogue: 0,0:44:05.86,0:44:09.87,Default,,0,0,0,,You show up here making wild accusations.\NIt’s blackmail. Charlatan!
Dialogue: 0,0:44:11.29,0:44:17.00,Default,,0,0,0,,Why did Fuyuko come that day?\NDid you ever find out?
Dialogue: 0,0:44:17.21,0:44:19.13,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:44:20.59,0:44:24.92,Default,,0,0,0,,Fuyuko must have been surprised\Nby how much Yukari and...
Dialogue: 0,0:44:25.13,0:44:27.76,Default,,0,0,0,,her own daughter looked alike.
Dialogue: 0,0:44:29.76,0:44:34.02,Default,,0,0,0,,"I apologize for the commotion.
Dialogue: 0,0:44:34.27,0:44:42.36,Default,,0,0,0,,"I, Koyuki Yamauchi, killed my\Nolder brother Toshio Yamauchi."
Dialogue: 0,0:44:44.28,0:44:50.03,Default,,0,0,0,,This letter was in the police mailbox\Nthis morning.
Dialogue: 0,0:44:50.37,0:44:54.75,Default,,0,0,0,,It is addressed to the Hospital Hill\NInvestigation Unit.
Dialogue: 0,0:44:55.00,0:45:00.54,Default,,0,0,0,,Koyuki Yamauchi signed\Nher name on the back.
Dialogue: 0,0:45:00.75,0:45:04.84,Default,,0,0,0,,Sagawa and every other member\Nof {\i1}The Angry Pirates{\i0}...
Dialogue: 0,0:45:04.88,0:45:08.97,Default,,0,0,0,,confirmed that it is indeed\NKoyuki’s handwriting.
Dialogue: 0,0:45:09.59,0:45:14.89,Default,,0,0,0,,The cancellation mark on the postage stamp suggests\Nit was sent the day after the incident.
Dialogue: 0,0:45:16.39,0:45:22.27,Default,,0,0,0,,This is why I asked you all\Nto come here today.
Dialogue: 0,0:45:22.27,0:45:24.65,Default,,0,0,0,,- Er...\N- What?
Dialogue: 0,0:45:24.86,0:45:29.20,Default,,0,0,0,,Yayoi was unable to attend\Ndue to a meeting at the hospital.
Dialogue: 0,0:45:30.20,0:45:33.91,Default,,0,0,0,,- What about that gumshoe?\N- I don’t know his address.
Dialogue: 0,0:45:34.37,0:45:36.62,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, who cares about him?
Dialogue: 0,0:45:37.12,0:45:42.84,Default,,0,0,0,,Regarding the motive for\Nthe murder, it says,
Dialogue: 0,0:45:43.71,0:45:49.93,Default,,0,0,0,,"We were brother and sister,\Neven though we were not related.
Dialogue: 0,0:45:50.34,0:45:55.01,Default,,0,0,0,,"His passionate love for me\Nwas a surprise,
Dialogue: 0,0:45:55.22,0:45:59.48,Default,,0,0,0,,"and although I agreed to marry him,
Dialogue: 0,0:45:59.69,0:46:03.65,Default,,0,0,0,,"as Toshio’s love grew more\Nand more intense,
Dialogue: 0,0:46:04.15,0:46:09.86,Default,,0,0,0,,"I could only see misery in our future.
Dialogue: 0,0:46:10.07,0:46:14.16,Default,,0,0,0,,"I suggested that we should break up,
Dialogue: 0,0:46:14.49,0:46:18.45,Default,,0,0,0,,"but I had no idea that he\Nwould react as he did.
Dialogue: 0,0:46:19.00,0:46:24.13,Default,,0,0,0,,"Toshio flew into a rage and\Nwouldn’t let me go.
Dialogue: 0,0:46:25.25,0:46:30.76,Default,,0,0,0,,"When he calmed down,\Nwe started to argue.
Dialogue: 0,0:46:31.01,0:46:35.55,Default,,0,0,0,,"I unwittingly stabbed him with\Na pair of scissors.
Dialogue: 0,0:46:35.81,0:46:39.98,Default,,0,0,0,,"Before I knew it,\NToshio was covered...
Dialogue: 0,0:46:40.14,0:46:42.85,Default,,0,0,0,,"in blood and near death.
Dialogue: 0,0:46:43.52,0:46:50.69,Default,,0,0,0,,"With his dying breath,\NToshio said that I should cut off his head,
Dialogue: 0,0:46:50.69,0:46:58.74,Default,,0,0,0,,"and hang it in the Hogen house from\Nthe chandelier, like a wind chime.
Dialogue: 0,0:46:59.25,0:47:04.33,Default,,0,0,0,,"With these, his dying words,\NI sought revenge on the house...
Dialogue: 0,0:47:04.54,0:47:08.75,Default,,0,0,0,,"that brought about\Nmy mother’s death.
Dialogue: 0,0:47:08.96,0:47:14.51,Default,,0,0,0,,"The wedding photo taken in the house\Nstemmed from similar motives.
Dialogue: 0,0:47:14.72,0:47:19.31,Default,,0,0,0,,"I believe that Toshio was seeking\Nto place a curse on the Hogen family.
Dialogue: 0,0:47:19.56,0:47:23.48,Default,,0,0,0,,"I made the decision to follow through\Nwith his request in the garage.
Dialogue: 0,0:47:23.77,0:47:29.53,Default,,0,0,0,,"A holy ceremony.\NI will follow Toshio to my mother’s side.
Dialogue: 0,0:47:29.57,0:47:33.74,Default,,0,0,0,,"Please disregard me as\Nan unfortunate girl and don’t look for me."
Dialogue: 0,0:47:33.86,0:47:38.08,Default,,0,0,0,,"I ask that you let me sleep\Nin eternal repose.
Dialogue: 0,0:47:38.83,0:47:41.20,Default,,0,0,0,,"Signed Koyuki Yamauchi."
Dialogue: 0,0:47:41.66,0:47:43.79,Default,,0,0,0,,That’s all she wrote.
Dialogue: 0,0:47:44.62,0:47:47.84,Default,,0,0,0,,This dispels all doubts about\NSagawa’s story.
Dialogue: 0,0:47:48.04,0:47:50.30,Default,,0,0,0,,Koyuki acted alone.
Dialogue: 0,0:47:50.63,0:47:54.18,Default,,0,0,0,,- If that’s so...\N- What?
Dialogue: 0,0:47:54.26,0:47:56.80,Default,,0,0,0,,Are you saying the case is solved?
Dialogue: 0,0:47:56.89,0:48:01.97,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes, once Koyuki’s body and\NToshio’s torso are recovered.
Dialogue: 0,0:48:24.16,0:48:25.46,Default,,0,0,0,,Who’s there?
Dialogue: 0,0:48:28.71,0:48:31.13,Default,,0,0,0,,What the…
Dialogue: 0,0:48:31.38,0:48:35.97,Default,,0,0,0,,Mr. Kindaichi, you startled me.
Dialogue: 0,0:48:36.26,0:48:39.85,Default,,0,0,0,,- You’re the one who scared {\i1}me{\i0}.\N- What are you doing here?
Dialogue: 0,0:48:40.10,0:48:42.85,Default,,0,0,0,,Looking for something.\NHow about you?
Dialogue: 0,0:48:43.10,0:48:46.19,Default,,0,0,0,,- To investigate.\N- You’re a private eye?
Dialogue: 0,0:48:46.81,0:48:48.94,Default,,0,0,0,,Check this out...
Dialogue: 0,0:48:54.07,0:48:56.11,Default,,0,0,0,,A brand new hypodermic needle.
Dialogue: 0,0:48:56.36,0:48:58.91,Default,,0,0,0,,- Where’d you find it?\N- Right over there.
Dialogue: 0,0:48:59.12,0:49:03.58,Default,,0,0,0,,I thought there might be physical evidence,\Nso I came to take a look.
Dialogue: 0,0:49:03.79,0:49:05.87,Default,,0,0,0,,When I checked this needle\Nfor trace drugs,
Dialogue: 0,0:49:06.08,0:49:08.87,Default,,0,0,0,,I discovered the bride was\Nnot of sound mind.
Dialogue: 0,0:49:09.08,0:49:11.79,Default,,0,0,0,,That is to say,\Nit wasn't an ordinary wedding.
Dialogue: 0,0:49:12.38,0:49:14.59,Default,,0,0,0,,You’re very dedicated.
Dialogue: 0,0:49:14.76,0:49:16.67,Default,,0,0,0,,This is fun for me.
Dialogue: 0,0:49:17.84,0:49:19.89,Default,,0,0,0,,And another thing,
Dialogue: 0,0:49:20.09,0:49:23.72,Default,,0,0,0,,I can’t forget the eyes of the girl\Nwho came to the studio that night.
Dialogue: 0,0:49:24.93,0:49:27.98,Default,,0,0,0,,Koyuki sent a suicide note\Nto the police.
Dialogue: 0,0:49:28.81,0:49:32.61,Default,,0,0,0,,She copped to everything,\Nand said that she planned to die, too.
Dialogue: 0,0:49:33.48,0:49:35.15,Default,,0,0,0,,What do you make of it?
Dialogue: 0,0:49:35.19,0:49:37.74,Default,,0,0,0,,I think the whole thing stinks.
Dialogue: 0,0:49:38.24,0:49:41.87,Default,,0,0,0,,That’s why I checked into\Nthe Hogen’s family tree.
Dialogue: 0,0:49:41.95,0:49:43.12,Default,,0,0,0,,The family tree?
Dialogue: 0,0:49:43.16,0:49:45.79,Default,,0,0,0,,Above and beyond what came out\Nfrom the police investigation.
Dialogue: 0,0:49:46.00,0:49:49.12,Default,,0,0,0,,I knew that I had to find out\Nwho the Hogens were.
Dialogue: 0,0:49:49.50,0:49:53.46,Default,,0,0,0,,The Hogens are a line of imperial doctors\Nfrom Iwate Prefecture.
Dialogue: 0,0:49:53.67,0:49:56.21,Default,,0,0,0,,They moved here in 1868.
Dialogue: 0,0:49:57.05,0:50:00.84,Default,,0,0,0,,The first son of the family\Nat the time was Tetsuma.
Dialogue: 0,0:50:00.89,0:50:03.60,Default,,0,0,0,,He set up the hospital here.
Dialogue: 0,0:50:03.80,0:50:06.77,Default,,0,0,0,,Tetsuma had a half-sister named Chizu due to\Nhis father’s dalliances, who was a real betty.
Dialogue: 0,0:50:06.85,0:50:10.06,Default,,0,0,0,,She had an illegitimate baby girl\Nwith one of the doctors.
Dialogue: 0,0:50:10.10,0:50:13.86,Default,,0,0,0,,That girl is Yayoi.\NWhen Chizu’s illicit lover died,
Dialogue: 0,0:50:14.02,0:50:18.11,Default,,0,0,0,,there was another guy, Mozo Igarashi,\Nwho was madly in love with her.
Dialogue: 0,0:50:18.49,0:50:21.45,Default,,0,0,0,,Chizu married Mozo and continued\Nto raise Yayoi.
Dialogue: 0,0:50:21.66,0:50:27.95,Default,,0,0,0,,When Yayoi came of age, she married\NTetsuma Hogen’s adopted son, Takuya.
Dialogue: 0,0:50:28.12,0:50:30.92,Default,,0,0,0,,Meanwhile, Mozo Igarashi and Chizu\Nhad a boy named Taizo.
Dialogue: 0,0:50:31.00,0:50:35.25,Default,,0,0,0,,The son of the maid\NMitsue Tanabe is Shigeru.
Dialogue: 0,0:50:35.50,0:50:38.05,Default,,0,0,0,,This is getting a little complicated.\NAre you following along?
Dialogue: 0,0:50:38.13,0:50:39.67,Default,,0,0,0,,Not really.
Dialogue: 0,0:50:39.72,0:50:44.18,Default,,0,0,0,,Yeah, I’m pretty confused myself.\NThat’s why I made a chart.
Dialogue: 0,0:50:47.77,0:50:52.23,Default,,0,0,0,,You can see that Chizu Hogen\Ntook her daughter Yayoi,
Dialogue: 0,0:50:52.48,0:50:55.40,Default,,0,0,0,,and married Mozo Igarashi.
Dialogue: 0,0:50:56.36,0:51:02.66,Default,,0,0,0,,Yayoi then married her cousin\NTakuya Hogen.
Dialogue: 0,0:51:03.32,0:51:05.70,Default,,0,0,0,,Their daughter is Yukari.
Dialogue: 0,0:51:07.37,0:51:11.25,Default,,0,0,0,,I see...\NWhere did you get this information?
Dialogue: 0,0:51:11.37,0:51:14.25,Default,,0,0,0,,A nurse at the Hogen Hospital told me.
Dialogue: 0,0:51:15.75,0:51:17.67,Default,,0,0,0,,It was easy enough to find out,
Dialogue: 0,0:51:18.09,0:51:22.30,Default,,0,0,0,,but people’s family histories\Nsure can get messy.
Dialogue: 0,0:51:24.22,0:51:30.85,Default,,0,0,0,,This chart shows that Takuya Hogen\Nhad Toshio and Koyuki with Fuyuko.
Dialogue: 0,0:51:31.60,0:51:35.73,Default,,0,0,0,,Their tragedy was the product of\Nan unfortunate lineage...
Dialogue: 0,0:51:35.73,0:51:40.82,Default,,0,0,0,,and an inconvenient birth.\NThey were also war orphans.
Dialogue: 0,0:51:41.44,0:51:43.74,Default,,0,0,0,,Me, too.
Dialogue: 0,0:51:44.07,0:51:47.45,Default,,0,0,0,,I was wandering from job to job\Nuntil Tokubei hired me.
Dialogue: 0,0:51:47.70,0:51:51.66,Default,,0,0,0,,- Really?\N- It’s no big deal.
Dialogue: 0,0:51:52.33,0:51:55.25,Default,,0,0,0,,Won’t you be fired for dawdling\Nhere with me?
Dialogue: 0,0:51:55.50,0:51:57.63,Default,,0,0,0,,I don’t care;\Njobs are easy to come by.
Dialogue: 0,0:51:58.42,0:52:02.72,Default,,0,0,0,,And plus, I think the photography studio\Nneeds me more than I need them.
Dialogue: 0,0:52:02.88,0:52:06.39,Default,,0,0,0,,Really. Is Naokichi married?
Dialogue: 0,0:52:07.30,0:52:11.22,Default,,0,0,0,,He was shot through the hip\Nin the war.
Dialogue: 0,0:52:11.35,0:52:13.56,Default,,0,0,0,,I think he’s impotent.
Dialogue: 0,0:52:15.27,0:52:20.52,Default,,0,0,0,,And Koyuki’s suicide note:\Ndid they find her fingerprints?
Dialogue: 0,0:52:20.69,0:52:23.99,Default,,0,0,0,,I don’t know.
Dialogue: 0,0:52:24.70,0:52:26.16,Default,,0,0,0,,I gotta go!
Dialogue: 0,0:52:26.57,0:52:28.32,Default,,0,0,0,,Mr. Kindaichi, where are you going?
Dialogue: 0,0:52:43.59,0:52:47.30,Default,,0,0,0,,We have a lot of dry plates of\Nthe Hogen Hospital.
Dialogue: 0,0:52:47.38,0:52:50.43,Default,,0,0,0,,They’ve been steady customers\Nfor three generations.
Dialogue: 0,0:52:51.47,0:52:56.14,Default,,0,0,0,,I saw you looking at a blueprint\Nthe other day...
Dialogue: 0,0:53:00.15,0:53:03.94,Default,,0,0,0,,You don’t tell me anything.
Dialogue: 0,0:53:05.86,0:53:08.61,Default,,0,0,0,,Where the hell have you been?!\NI guess you forgot we've an on-location shoot.
Dialogue: 0,0:53:08.66,0:53:12.12,Default,,0,0,0,,- Sorry.\N- You have work?
Dialogue: 0,0:53:12.95,0:53:15.41,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes, a large wedding reception.
Dialogue: 0,0:53:15.91,0:53:17.96,Default,,0,0,0,,They said that...
Dialogue: 0,0:53:18.21,0:53:20.13,Default,,0,0,0,,Hey, get ready!
Dialogue: 0,0:53:21.59,0:53:24.13,Default,,0,0,0,,…they’ll also need an assistant.
Dialogue: 0,0:53:25.88,0:53:27.80,Default,,0,0,0,,As I was saying,
Dialogue: 0,0:53:28.26,0:53:31.30,Default,,0,0,0,,are you going to build a building?
Dialogue: 0,0:53:31.47,0:53:33.31,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:53:35.31,0:53:39.85,Default,,0,0,0,,Naokichi, this is no time to cling\Nto tradition.
Dialogue: 0,0:53:40.35,0:53:42.77,Default,,0,0,0,,I have new plans.
Dialogue: 0,0:53:43.73,0:53:48.65,Default,,0,0,0,,I want to renovate the old building into\Nan eight-story structure.
Dialogue: 0,0:53:49.07,0:53:53.03,Default,,0,0,0,,We'll be able to hold all\Nwedding events there.
Dialogue: 0,0:53:53.78,0:53:57.71,Default,,0,0,0,,We'll have a large reception area and\Nrestaurant on the first floor.
Dialogue: 0,0:53:57.75,0:54:00.88,Default,,0,0,0,,On the second floor,\Nwe'll have Shinto, Buddhist...
Dialogue: 0,0:54:00.92,0:54:04.13,Default,,0,0,0,,and Christian wedding halls,\Nas well as a beauty parlor.
Dialogue: 0,0:54:04.21,0:54:09.05,Default,,0,0,0,,Of course, we'll also have\Na modern photography studio.
Dialogue: 0,0:54:10.26,0:54:15.14,Default,,0,0,0,,I really want both a large and\Na small wedding reception hall.
Dialogue: 0,0:54:15.43,0:54:17.31,Default,,0,0,0,,That would be grand...
Dialogue: 0,0:54:18.31,0:54:21.65,Default,,0,0,0,,But where are you going to\Nget the money?
Dialogue: 0,0:54:21.73,0:54:24.73,Default,,0,0,0,,You're always futzing around,\Nso I'll have to take care of everything.
Dialogue: 0,0:54:24.94,0:54:28.86,Default,,0,0,0,,- Just you wait and see.\N- OK, Naokichi, I’m ready.
Dialogue: 0,0:54:29.20,0:54:30.45,Default,,0,0,0,,Let’s go.
Dialogue: 0,0:54:34.24,0:54:36.20,Default,,0,0,0,,What’re you rubbernecking at?
Dialogue: 0,0:54:36.91,0:54:39.00,Default,,0,0,0,,- Are you going to go like that?\N- Yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:54:39.21,0:54:41.71,Default,,0,0,0,,It’s OK in this old building, but…
Dialogue: 0,0:54:41.87,0:54:43.71,Default,,0,0,0,,I’m sick of hearing about it!
Dialogue: 0,0:54:56.18,0:54:59.93,Default,,0,0,0,,Were Koyuki’s fingerprints found\Non the suicide note?
Dialogue: 0,0:55:00.02,0:55:03.02,Default,,0,0,0,,I understand that, being sent through the mail,\Nother people touched it. But still...
Dialogue: 0,0:55:03.06,0:55:04.31,Default,,0,0,0,,Fingerprints?
Dialogue: 0,0:55:04.52,0:55:07.98,Default,,0,0,0,,If you haven’t dusted for them,\Nplease do so.
Dialogue: 0,0:55:25.96,0:55:29.71,Default,,0,0,0,,Sir, we found no fingerprints\Nwhatsoever on the stationery!
Dialogue: 0,0:55:29.92,0:55:31.34,Default,,0,0,0,,What?!
Dialogue: 0,0:55:36.93,0:55:40.22,Default,,0,0,0,,Maybe Koyuki wrote the note\Nwith gloves on.
Dialogue: 0,0:55:40.47,0:55:42.43,Default,,0,0,0,,Why would she bother?
Dialogue: 0,0:55:42.69,0:55:46.27,Default,,0,0,0,,Come to think of it, two sets of\Nfingerprints were found at the garage.
Dialogue: 0,0:55:46.48,0:55:48.86,Default,,0,0,0,,One was determined to be those\Nof the drummer Sagawa,
Dialogue: 0,0:55:50.36,0:55:52.40,Default,,0,0,0,,and the other belonged to\Nthe trumpeter Toshio.
Dialogue: 0,0:55:52.61,0:55:56.24,Default,,0,0,0,,Which means that Koyuki’s fingerprints\Nare not on anything related to the case.
Dialogue: 0,0:55:56.41,0:56:00.12,Default,,0,0,0,,But Koyuki had been living in\Nthe garage until the murder.
Dialogue: 0,0:56:00.33,0:56:04.75,Default,,0,0,0,,It doesn’t add up. Could she or\Nsomeone else have wiped them down?
Dialogue: 0,0:56:42.12,0:56:45.41,Default,,0,0,0,,- I thought I was alone.\N- I never left.
Dialogue: 0,0:56:45.66,0:56:47.75,Default,,0,0,0,,Really?
Dialogue: 0,0:56:52.30,0:56:59.47,Default,,0,0,0,,It’s been a while since you burned\Nincense for your husband.
Dialogue: 0,0:57:05.06,0:57:07.44,Default,,0,0,0,,By the way,\NMr. Kindaichi is here.
Dialogue: 0,0:57:22.79,0:57:24.66,Default,,0,0,0,,I’m sorry for the wait.
Dialogue: 0,0:57:25.12,0:57:28.21,Default,,0,0,0,,Is this house a part of the hospital?
Dialogue: 0,0:57:28.58,0:57:32.71,Default,,0,0,0,,The hospital was destroyed\Nin the war,
Dialogue: 0,0:57:32.92,0:57:35.46,Default,,0,0,0,,so we rebuilt the hospital\Nadjoining the house.
Dialogue: 0,0:57:36.26,0:57:40.93,Default,,0,0,0,,I’d like to ask you about\NKoyuki’s suicide note.
Dialogue: 0,0:57:41.14,0:57:43.68,Default,,0,0,0,,It was quite a surprise.
Dialogue: 0,0:57:44.77,0:57:49.52,Default,,0,0,0,,Koyuki and Yukari were half-sisters,\Nand I thought of her as a daughter.
Dialogue: 0,0:57:49.77,0:57:53.23,Default,,0,0,0,,I thought she probably hated me,
Dialogue: 0,0:57:53.44,0:57:58.03,Default,,0,0,0,,since her mother died\Nright after she came here.
Dialogue: 0,0:57:58.95,0:58:04.12,Default,,0,0,0,,I thought your husband’s\Nsheet music might be here.
Dialogue: 0,0:58:04.41,0:58:06.41,Default,,0,0,0,,Why do you ask?
Dialogue: 0,0:58:07.71,0:58:11.88,Default,,0,0,0,,Does it have anything to do\Nwith Koyuki?
Dialogue: 0,0:58:12.88,0:58:16.34,Default,,0,0,0,,The strip of paper at the murder site\Nhad a song written on it.
Dialogue: 0,0:58:16.55,0:58:19.63,Default,,0,0,0,,I think it had something to do with\NFuyuko and her children.
Dialogue: 0,0:58:19.97,0:58:23.51,Default,,0,0,0,,So if there are any others,\NI’d like to see them.
Dialogue: 0,0:58:24.14,0:58:28.52,Default,,0,0,0,,I never had any interest in\Nmy husband’s music.
Dialogue: 0,0:58:28.73,0:58:33.23,Default,,0,0,0,,I assume his written music was\Ndestroyed in the war.
Dialogue: 0,0:58:36.23,0:58:40.07,Default,,0,0,0,,- A policeman is here.\N- I’m sorry to disturb you.
Dialogue: 0,0:58:40.11,0:58:42.66,Default,,0,0,0,,I’m glad to have found you here.
Dialogue: 0,0:58:43.03,0:58:46.12,Default,,0,0,0,,Didn’t Tokubei Honjo hire you for\Nan investigation?
Dialogue: 0,0:58:46.16,0:58:49.29,Default,,0,0,0,,- Yes.\N- What for?
Dialogue: 0,0:58:49.50,0:58:51.71,Default,,0,0,0,,He had an accident at an empty building.
Dialogue: 0,0:58:51.79,0:58:54.17,Default,,0,0,0,,Tokubei Honjo has been murdered!
Dialogue: 0,0:59:06.93,0:59:09.60,Default,,0,0,0,,He was killed at the\Nphotography studio.
Dialogue: 0,0:59:10.73,0:59:14.61,Default,,0,0,0,,- When?\N- Today at around 1:00pm.
Dialogue: 0,0:59:15.44,0:59:21.24,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Naokichi and Mokutaro came home\Nto find the red light on in the dark room,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:59:21.49,0:59:25.07,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}even though the door was open.\NWhen they looked inside,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:59:25.24,0:59:30.20,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}they found Tokubei dead,\Nwith his head in the basin.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:59:30.37,0:59:35.96,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}His head was bashed open\Nwith a water dish,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:59:36.17,0:59:39.05,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}and he had drowned.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:59:39.38,0:59:43.72,Default,,0,0,0,,The direct cause of death\Nwas suffocation.
Dialogue: 0,0:59:45.01,0:59:48.26,Default,,0,0,0,,According to testimony from\NNaokichi and Mokutaro,
Dialogue: 0,0:59:48.43,0:59:51.06,Default,,0,0,0,,they were photographing\Na wedding reception.
Dialogue: 0,0:59:51.10,0:59:54.73,Default,,0,0,0,,However, when they arrived at\Nthe designated place,
Dialogue: 0,0:59:54.73,0:59:58.90,Default,,0,0,0,,they found that there was\Nin fact no reception being held.
Dialogue: 0,0:59:59.19,1:00:01.61,Default,,0,0,0,,Thus we can conclude that...
Dialogue: 0,1:00:01.65,1:00:05.53,Default,,0,0,0,,the perpetrator made the appointment\Nso he could carry out his sinister crime.
Dialogue: 0,1:00:05.66,1:00:06.99,Default,,0,0,0,,Who made the appointment?
Dialogue: 0,1:00:07.37,1:00:09.45,Default,,0,0,0,,It was evidently a man.
Dialogue: 0,1:00:10.58,1:00:16.42,Default,,0,0,0,,I’d like to ask you about your relationship\Nto the Honjo Photography Studio?
Dialogue: 0,1:00:16.83,1:00:21.76,Default,,0,0,0,,I only ask because,\Nafter the killer dispatched Tokubei,
Dialogue: 0,1:00:21.96,1:00:25.26,Default,,0,0,0,,he took all of the old dry plates\Nbeing stored there,
Dialogue: 0,1:00:25.30,1:00:28.39,Default,,0,0,0,,and smashed those related\Nto your family.
Dialogue: 0,1:00:29.31,1:00:34.89,Default,,0,0,0,,Naokichi and Mokutaro said that the\NHogen family had always been a customer,
Dialogue: 0,1:00:35.14,1:00:39.57,Default,,0,0,0,,but beyond this,\Nthey couldn’t say.
Dialogue: 0,1:00:41.32,1:00:47.20,Default,,0,0,0,,Aside from the fact that we've taken\Nour photos at the Honjo studio,
Dialogue: 0,1:00:47.41,1:00:51.08,Default,,0,0,0,,I can’t think of anything.
Dialogue: 0,1:00:51.24,1:00:53.16,Default,,0,0,0,,I see.
Dialogue: 0,1:00:54.16,1:00:58.54,Default,,0,0,0,,Still, I can’t believe that this was\Na simple matter of larceny.
Dialogue: 0,1:01:07.97,1:01:10.55,Default,,0,0,0,,There’s a strange sound coming\Nfrom the ceiling.
Dialogue: 0,1:01:12.77,1:01:15.23,Default,,0,0,0,,We use the attic for storage.
Dialogue: 0,1:01:15.39,1:01:19.19,Default,,0,0,0,,- Is there anyone else here?\N- Mice, I imagine.
Dialogue: 0,1:01:19.40,1:01:21.40,Default,,0,0,0,,- What? Oh, yes.\N- See?!
Dialogue: 0,1:01:22.15,1:01:25.82,Default,,0,0,0,,In any event, I need you to investigate\Nthat empty building.
Dialogue: 0,1:01:27.07,1:01:32.83,Default,,0,0,0,,Did you come to check out the building\Nwithout the superintendent, Kindaichi?
Dialogue: 0,1:01:32.83,1:01:39.13,Default,,0,0,0,,- Yes. - I’ve never met, seen, spoken\Nor eaten with this man before.
Dialogue: 0,1:01:39.25,1:01:42.04,Default,,0,0,0,,The night I went to inform Tokubei of\Nthe results of my investigation,
Dialogue: 0,1:01:42.25,1:01:45.13,Default,,0,0,0,,was the night that the\Nsevered head was discovered.
Dialogue: 0,1:01:45.59,1:01:48.18,Default,,0,0,0,,There was evidence that the building\Nhad been tampered with.
Dialogue: 0,1:01:50.26,1:01:51.72,Default,,0,0,0,,There are nail holes in the ceiling.
Dialogue: 0,1:01:52.72,1:01:55.77,Default,,0,0,0,,The trap was actually quite simple.
Dialogue: 0,1:01:56.23,1:01:58.60,Default,,0,0,0,,That’s quite a heavy wind chime.
Dialogue: 0,1:02:12.45,1:02:15.16,Default,,0,0,0,,I feel like I saved his life.
Dialogue: 0,1:02:16.12,1:02:19.50,Default,,0,0,0,,If I hadn’t called out to him,
Dialogue: 0,1:02:19.71,1:02:26.34,Default,,0,0,0,,the wind chimes would’ve fallen\Ndirectly on him.
Dialogue: 0,1:02:26.96,1:02:31.80,Default,,0,0,0,,That’s true. And if you'd entered\Nthe building first, you might've died.
Dialogue: 0,1:02:32.34,1:02:34.05,Default,,0,0,0,,I hadn’t thought of that.
Dialogue: 0,1:02:34.14,1:02:36.43,Default,,0,0,0,,Hey, what happened to the wind chimes?
Dialogue: 0,1:02:36.64,1:02:41.65,Default,,0,0,0,,I don’t know. We we’re both so surprised,\Nwe went straight home.
Dialogue: 0,1:02:41.81,1:02:43.90,Default,,0,0,0,,The crime was planned.
Dialogue: 0,1:02:45.23,1:02:50.91,Default,,0,0,0,,Why would the perpetrator have known\NTokubei would enter this building on that day?
Dialogue: 0,1:02:51.11,1:02:55.03,Default,,0,0,0,,That’s right.\NNeither Naokichi nor Mokutaro knew.
Dialogue: 0,1:02:55.70,1:02:59.79,Default,,0,0,0,,- Did you tell anyone that\NTokubei was coming? - No.
Dialogue: 0,1:03:00.08,1:03:01.54,Default,,0,0,0,,Who owns this building?
Dialogue: 0,1:03:01.75,1:03:05.75,Default,,0,0,0,,I hear that it’s the Public Welfare\NDivision of the Hogen Hospital.
Dialogue: 0,1:03:07.92,1:03:10.34,Default,,0,0,0,,Did something happen to Tokubei?
Dialogue: 0,1:03:10.59,1:03:13.47,Default,,0,0,0,,- He was murdered!\N- Oh.
Dialogue: 0,1:03:38.79,1:03:40.50,Default,,0,0,0,,Koyuki.
Dialogue: 0,1:03:54.01,1:03:56.76,Default,,0,0,0,,I don’t see any books of interest.
Dialogue: 0,1:03:57.56,1:04:00.02,Default,,0,0,0,,They’re not in any\Nparticular order, either.
Dialogue: 0,1:04:01.06,1:04:04.15,Default,,0,0,0,,Technical books and literature\Nare mixed together.
Dialogue: 0,1:04:04.35,1:04:06.61,Default,,0,0,0,,Maybe they could be ordered by height.
Dialogue: 0,1:04:07.44,1:04:09.69,Default,,0,0,0,,The store’s dark, too.
Dialogue: 0,1:04:10.57,1:04:15.61,Default,,0,0,0,,Maybe so, but used bookstores\Ndon’t make much money.
Dialogue: 0,1:04:15.87,1:04:19.16,Default,,0,0,0,,They deal in culture.
Dialogue: 0,1:04:19.33,1:04:24.08,Default,,0,0,0,,This store hasn’t even got the most\Npopular titles. What a crummy shop!
Dialogue: 0,1:04:24.54,1:04:27.29,Default,,0,0,0,,Hey, watch your mouth.
Dialogue: 0,1:04:28.17,1:04:30.80,Default,,0,0,0,,This is my store.
Dialogue: 0,1:04:32.01,1:04:34.55,Default,,0,0,0,,I’m terribly sorry.
Dialogue: 0,1:04:35.47,1:04:37.97,Default,,0,0,0,,I own this store.
Dialogue: 0,1:04:38.93,1:04:44.52,Default,,0,0,0,,I heard your bookstore was the best place\Nto find old books about this region.
Dialogue: 0,1:04:44.73,1:04:48.31,Default,,0,0,0,,Do you have any songbooks\Nby Takuya Hogen?
Dialogue: 0,1:04:48.52,1:04:53.24,Default,,0,0,0,,You’re asking for a single book.\NDo you think I know every book in the store?
Dialogue: 0,1:04:54.32,1:04:56.45,Default,,0,0,0,,Do you know the Hogen Hospital?
Dialogue: 0,1:04:56.82,1:05:00.62,Default,,0,0,0,,Yeah, it’s the best hospital in the area.
Dialogue: 0,1:05:00.70,1:05:03.33,Default,,0,0,0,,I’m looking for a book of songs written\Nby the former director of the hospital.
Dialogue: 0,1:05:03.58,1:05:06.79,Default,,0,0,0,,A book of songs...
Dialogue: 0,1:05:07.54,1:05:17.38,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}The ruins of an old castle,\Nwhite clouds and a sad traveler...{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:05:17.68,1:05:20.89,Default,,0,0,0,,I like the old songs;\Nthey had rhythm.
Dialogue: 0,1:05:21.14,1:05:25.73,Default,,0,0,0,,"I worked like a dog,\Nbut my life was pleasant."
Dialogue: 0,1:05:26.39,1:05:30.65,Default,,0,0,0,,"I Stare at my Hand,"\NTakuboku Ishikawa.
Dialogue: 0,1:05:30.94,1:05:33.28,Default,,0,0,0,,I know just how he feels.
Dialogue: 0,1:05:34.28,1:05:39.07,Default,,0,0,0,,Nowadays music doesn’t have\Nflavor or feeling. I don’t like it.
Dialogue: 0,1:05:39.53,1:05:42.20,Default,,0,0,0,,No, what I’m trying to say is…
Dialogue: 0,1:05:42.54,1:05:43.95,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Mr. Kindaichi.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:05:46.41,1:05:48.79,Default,,0,0,0,,Fancy meeting you here.
Dialogue: 0,1:05:50.79,1:05:53.00,Default,,0,0,0,,Why are you still in Japan?
Dialogue: 0,1:05:55.34,1:05:57.38,Default,,0,0,0,,The old man just said...
Dialogue: 0,1:05:57.63,1:06:01.85,Default,,0,0,0,,the other day that you were probably\Nsailing on the Pacific Ocean by now.
Dialogue: 0,1:06:02.01,1:06:05.85,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, that….
Dialogue: 0,1:06:06.60,1:06:10.48,Default,,0,0,0,,Hey, did you find the book?
Dialogue: 0,1:06:10.65,1:06:12.11,Default,,0,0,0,,Not yet.
Dialogue: 0,1:06:12.31,1:06:15.44,Default,,0,0,0,,Kindaichi, the police don’t think that...
Dialogue: 0,1:06:15.65,1:06:18.74,Default,,0,0,0,,Tokubei’s death and\NToshio’s murder are related.
Dialogue: 0,1:06:18.78,1:06:21.37,Default,,0,0,0,,- Really?\N- I don’t buy it.
Dialogue: 0,1:06:21.53,1:06:26.04,Default,,0,0,0,,The Hogen family's dry plates were smashed.\NIt had to have something to do with the Hogens.
Dialogue: 0,1:06:26.20,1:06:30.50,Default,,0,0,0,,Are you investigating the severed head/\Nwind chime incident, Kindaichi?
Dialogue: 0,1:06:30.71,1:06:32.79,Default,,0,0,0,,You could say that.
Dialogue: 0,1:06:33.00,1:06:35.50,Default,,0,0,0,,- Who’s she?\N- She’s a pharmacy student.
Dialogue: 0,1:06:35.71,1:06:38.17,Default,,0,0,0,,I recently met Mr. Kindaichi.\NMy name is Miss Sata.
Dialogue: 0,1:06:38.38,1:06:40.18,Default,,0,0,0,,- Miss Sata?\N- This is Mokutaro.
Dialogue: 0,1:06:40.22,1:06:43.10,Default,,0,0,0,,- Are you Mr. Kindaichi’s assistant?\N- No, it’s not like that.
Dialogue: 0,1:06:43.30,1:06:44.93,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes, it’s very much like that.
Dialogue: 0,1:06:45.72,1:06:48.73,Default,,0,0,0,,I don’t want to be involved in\Nany investigation,
Dialogue: 0,1:06:48.89,1:06:52.65,Default,,0,0,0,,but I feel like I’m being\Ndragged into one.
Dialogue: 0,1:06:53.02,1:06:56.07,Default,,0,0,0,,The old man wrote a detective novel\Nwith that kind of a sleuth.
Dialogue: 0,1:06:56.11,1:06:59.99,Default,,0,0,0,,- That’s not a private eye.\N- Still, it was a good book.
Dialogue: 0,1:07:00.03,1:07:06.24,Default,,0,0,0,,I was focusing on the danger posed by\Na person who mistook Yukari for Koyuki,
Dialogue: 0,1:07:06.29,1:07:08.54,Default,,0,0,0,,and in the meantime,\NTokubei was killed.
Dialogue: 0,1:07:08.54,1:07:13.00,Default,,0,0,0,,Do you think that I’m in danger?
Dialogue: 0,1:07:13.25,1:07:14.92,Default,,0,0,0,,It’s possible.
Dialogue: 0,1:07:15.13,1:07:18.46,Default,,0,0,0,,We must also consider the safety\Nof the {\i1}Angry Pirates{\i0}.
Dialogue: 0,1:07:18.51,1:07:20.84,Default,,0,0,0,,Then why did someone kill Tokubei?
Dialogue: 0,1:07:21.05,1:07:23.09,Default,,0,0,0,,When he saw the wedding photo,\Nhe thought it was Yukari.
Dialogue: 0,1:07:23.18,1:07:26.14,Default,,0,0,0,,I think Tokubei was killed\Nfor another reason,
Dialogue: 0,1:07:26.47,1:07:29.73,Default,,0,0,0,,and we can find that reason at\Nthe Honjo Photography Studio.
Dialogue: 0,1:07:29.93,1:07:32.27,Default,,0,0,0,,- The studio itself is under suspicion?\N- Yes.
Dialogue: 0,1:07:32.35,1:07:34.27,Default,,0,0,0,,Is this connected to the photographs?
Dialogue: 0,1:07:34.48,1:07:38.73,Default,,0,0,0,,The newspapers are reporting that the police\Ndeclared the severed head case closed.
Dialogue: 0,1:07:38.86,1:07:41.74,Default,,0,0,0,,But Koyuki’s body and Toshio’s torso\Nare still unaccounted for.
Dialogue: 0,1:07:41.82,1:07:44.66,Default,,0,0,0,,Then the case still seems open to me.
Dialogue: 0,1:07:45.07,1:07:50.50,Default,,0,0,0,,90% of the human body can be\Ndestroyed by chemicals;
Dialogue: 0,1:07:50.75,1:07:57.04,Default,,0,0,0,,the skin and internal organs\Nwill dissolve in sulfuric acid.
Dialogue: 0,1:07:57.09,1:08:04.01,Default,,0,0,0,,Bones placed in{\i1} aqua regia {\i0}can\Neasily be reduced to powder.
Dialogue: 0,1:08:04.22,1:08:08.81,Default,,0,0,0,,That’s why I think the perpetrator\Ndissolved the bodies with chemicals.
Dialogue: 0,1:08:11.18,1:08:13.39,Default,,0,0,0,,That’s quite a theory.
Dialogue: 0,1:08:13.60,1:08:15.19,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Hey, you.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:08:15.40,1:08:20.65,Default,,0,0,0,,This ain’t a tavern!\NI’m trying to run a business here.
Dialogue: 0,1:08:20.86,1:08:23.07,Default,,0,0,0,,Did you find the songbook?
Dialogue: 0,1:08:23.40,1:08:24.70,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, hey, honey.
Dialogue: 0,1:08:24.91,1:08:28.24,Default,,0,0,0,,Are you reading the merchandise again?\NI’m trying to run a business here!
Dialogue: 0,1:08:29.99,1:08:34.71,Default,,0,0,0,,Just a second...\N{\i1}Songs of Wind Chimes{\i0} by Takuya Hogen.
Dialogue: 0,1:08:34.75,1:08:39.00,Default,,0,0,0,,I was reading it all along!\NHey, I found your book.
Dialogue: 0,1:08:40.21,1:08:42.38,Default,,0,0,0,,Pretty good business, I’d say.
Dialogue: 0,1:08:44.84,1:08:49.01,Default,,0,0,0,,I want to see you right away.\NThere’s something I need to show you.
Dialogue: 0,1:08:49.22,1:08:52.81,Default,,0,0,0,,I can’t tell you on the phone.
Dialogue: 0,1:08:53.35,1:08:57.10,Default,,0,0,0,,You could call it my father’s\Ndying message.
Dialogue: 0,1:08:57.61,1:09:02.28,Default,,0,0,0,,It'll help you as much as me.
Dialogue: 0,1:09:02.49,1:09:05.45,Default,,0,0,0,,That’s ridiculous.\NI can’t comply.
Dialogue: 0,1:09:05.65,1:09:09.87,Default,,0,0,0,,Do you even know what you’re doing?\NThis is a clear criminal offense.
Dialogue: 0,1:09:09.91,1:09:12.08,Default,,0,0,0,,I want to talk to you as soon\Nas possible.
Dialogue: 0,1:09:12.29,1:09:16.12,Default,,0,0,0,,There’s someone involved that\Nwe hadn’t expected.
Dialogue: 0,1:09:17.17,1:09:20.84,Default,,0,0,0,,Where are you?
Dialogue: 0,1:09:21.09,1:09:23.26,Default,,0,0,0,,I don’t have anything to show you.
Dialogue: 0,1:09:23.46,1:09:27.30,Default,,0,0,0,,But it would be problematic\Nfor you if I knew.
Dialogue: 0,1:09:27.76,1:09:31.85,Default,,0,0,0,,I think it’s a perfectly reasonable demand.
Dialogue: 0,1:09:32.18,1:09:34.10,Default,,0,0,0,,There’s nobody here by that name.
Dialogue: 0,1:09:34.31,1:09:36.39,Default,,0,0,0,,Are you sure you’re not mistaken?
Dialogue: 0,1:09:36.64,1:09:37.94,Default,,0,0,0,,Who am I speaking to?
Dialogue: 0,1:09:37.98,1:09:40.11,Default,,0,0,0,,I can’t tell you. No way.
Dialogue: 0,1:09:40.31,1:09:43.94,Default,,0,0,0,,I understand the circumstances,\Nbut I can’t take responsibility.
Dialogue: 0,1:09:44.15,1:09:46.78,Default,,0,0,0,,Yeah, why?
Dialogue: 0,1:09:47.57,1:09:49.78,Default,,0,0,0,,Yeah, how come?
Dialogue: 0,1:09:52.24,1:09:54.70,Default,,0,0,0,,Are you trying to blackmail\Nan officer of the law?
Dialogue: 0,1:10:31.62,1:10:34.24,Default,,0,0,0,,Are you Shigeru Yoshizawa?
Dialogue: 0,1:10:38.29,1:10:41.79,Default,,0,0,0,,I have no intention of listening to you\Nbesmirch Yukari’s good name.
Dialogue: 0,1:10:42.33,1:10:46.46,Default,,0,0,0,,Then why did you agree to come?
Dialogue: 0,1:10:47.59,1:10:49.26,Default,,0,0,0,,The only reason you might've come...
Dialogue: 0,1:10:49.43,1:10:53.10,Default,,0,0,0,,is because you know I wasn’t lying\Nwhen I said that the girl wasn't Yukari.
Dialogue: 0,1:10:53.14,1:10:55.60,Default,,0,0,0,,- You’re running a con game.\N- I’m more honest than you.
Dialogue: 0,1:10:55.81,1:10:57.60,Default,,0,0,0,,I won’t be blackmailed by you!
Dialogue: 0,1:10:58.89,1:11:02.77,Default,,0,0,0,,Breathe another word and\Nthis will end badly for you!
Dialogue: 0,1:11:48.32,1:11:50.03,Default,,0,0,0,,Koyuki...
Dialogue: 0,1:11:52.24,1:11:56.58,Default,,0,0,0,,No one’s here,\Nso I can call you Koyuki.
Dialogue: 0,1:11:59.91,1:12:01.21,Default,,0,0,0,,Come here.
Dialogue: 0,1:12:17.01,1:12:18.56,Default,,0,0,0,,Be careful...
Dialogue: 0,1:12:19.47,1:12:24.56,Default,,0,0,0,,No matter what anyone says,\Nyou have to pretend to be Yukari.
Dialogue: 0,1:12:28.02,1:12:30.48,Default,,0,0,0,,I can’t take this anymore.
Dialogue: 0,1:12:31.69,1:12:34.07,Default,,0,0,0,,I’m scared something awful's\Ngoing to happen.
Dialogue: 0,1:12:34.28,1:12:39.87,Default,,0,0,0,,I plan to leave the house to you\Ninstead of Yukari.
Dialogue: 0,1:12:41.20,1:12:43.83,Default,,0,0,0,,Forget about Shigeru.
Dialogue: 0,1:12:45.33,1:12:50.13,Default,,0,0,0,,Your strong resemblance to Yukari...
Dialogue: 0,1:12:50.34,1:12:54.97,Default,,0,0,0,,is the only thing keeping\Nthis plan afloat.
Dialogue: 0,1:12:56.55,1:13:01.60,Default,,0,0,0,,This was only possible because you’re\Nthe spitting image of Yukari.
Dialogue: 0,1:13:02.77,1:13:08.27,Default,,0,0,0,,Your father wanted me to meet you.
Dialogue: 0,1:13:09.44,1:13:12.65,Default,,0,0,0,,That was his curse.
Dialogue: 0,1:13:12.69,1:13:17.62,Default,,0,0,0,,You looked too much like Yukari for him\Nto introduce us to each other.
Dialogue: 0,1:13:18.07,1:13:23.08,Default,,0,0,0,,I understood that when\NI finally met you.
Dialogue: 0,1:13:24.25,1:13:27.63,Default,,0,0,0,,My mother - I’m sorry.
Dialogue: 0,1:13:27.83,1:13:29.75,Default,,0,0,0,,Forget about that.
Dialogue: 0,1:13:31.38,1:13:36.68,Default,,0,0,0,,Even though Toshio wasn't\Na blood relation to Fuyuko…
Dialogue: 0,1:13:37.18,1:13:44.14,Default,,0,0,0,,He was much better to Mom\Nthan I was.
Dialogue: 0,1:13:44.98,1:13:51.11,Default,,0,0,0,,She was convinced my father would come\N{\i1}every time the wind chimes blew.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:13:51.32,1:13:54.90,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}She left the wind chimes up,\Neven in the winter.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:14:14.26,1:14:17.34,Default,,0,0,0,,Can you forget Toshio?
Dialogue: 0,1:14:19.18,1:14:24.77,Default,,0,0,0,,Toshio formed the jazz band\Nsoon after...
Dialogue: 0,1:14:24.97,1:14:28.89,Default,,0,0,0,,Fuyuko died and you left\Nthe property, didn’t he?
Dialogue: 0,1:14:29.06,1:14:30.27,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes.
Dialogue: 0,1:14:33.36,1:14:36.07,Default,,0,0,0,,We needed to eat.
Dialogue: 0,1:14:38.32,1:14:41.78,Default,,0,0,0,,And he always enjoyed music.
Dialogue: 0,1:14:43.66,1:14:49.17,Default,,0,0,0,,He always said that his mind went blank\Nwhen he played trumpet.
Dialogue: 0,1:14:50.75,1:14:53.84,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}We went traveling around\NUS military bases.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:14:55.00,1:14:57.84,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}It was a hard life.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:14:58.05,1:15:01.93,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I never imagined myself a singer,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:15:02.09,1:15:07.60,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}but I had to make ends meet.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:16:32.72,1:16:33.97,Default,,0,0,0,,Over here!
Dialogue: 0,1:16:37.51,1:16:39.60,Default,,0,0,0,,Sorry to be late.
Dialogue: 0,1:16:42.27,1:16:46.40,Default,,0,0,0,,I wanted to tell you,\NNaokichi has been acting funny recently.
Dialogue: 0,1:16:46.65,1:16:49.44,Default,,0,0,0,,He goes on little errands all the time\Nand it’s unrelated to work.
Dialogue: 0,1:16:49.48,1:16:52.40,Default,,0,0,0,,Has he been talking to anyone\Non the phone?
Dialogue: 0,1:16:52.61,1:16:54.70,Default,,0,0,0,,- I’m not sure.\N- I see.
Dialogue: 0,1:16:55.37,1:16:59.08,Default,,0,0,0,,It's a little early for dinner,\Nbut why don't you join me?
Dialogue: 0,1:16:59.29,1:17:01.12,Default,,0,0,0,,- I'll pay.\N- You don’t have to.
Dialogue: 0,1:17:01.29,1:17:03.79,Default,,0,0,0,,Don’t worry, I can expense it\Nas a private eye.
Dialogue: 0,1:17:04.00,1:17:07.79,Default,,0,0,0,,- Does that mean I'm a necessary\Nexpenditure? - Just like me.
Dialogue: 0,1:17:08.05,1:17:10.38,Default,,0,0,0,,- Excuse me!\N- What?
Dialogue: 0,1:17:10.42,1:17:15.22,Default,,0,0,0,,- Egg porridge and miso soup.\N- One egg gruel and pottage!
Dialogue: 0,1:17:16.60,1:17:17.76,Default,,0,0,0,,Mokutaro...
Dialogue: 0,1:17:18.72,1:17:22.85,Default,,0,0,0,,Takuya Hogen called this songbook,\N{\i1}The House of Wind Chimes{\i0}.
Dialogue: 0,1:17:23.31,1:17:26.98,Default,,0,0,0,,All of the songs are connected\Nwith the Yamauchi family.
Dialogue: 0,1:17:27.02,1:17:29.65,Default,,0,0,0,,This is a goldmine of information.
Dialogue: 0,1:17:29.86,1:17:32.86,Default,,0,0,0,,But what does it have to do with\Nthe investigation?
Dialogue: 0,1:17:33.07,1:17:39.08,Default,,0,0,0,,This book shows how unhappy Fuyuko was\Nto be separated from Toshio and Koyuki.
Dialogue: 0,1:17:39.12,1:17:41.66,Default,,0,0,0,,There are songs in the book\Nthat mention Koyuki?
Dialogue: 0,1:17:41.87,1:17:43.37,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes, several.
Dialogue: 0,1:17:43.79,1:17:49.09,Default,,0,0,0,,Unable to take care of his own daughter,\NTakuya entrusted Koyuki’s future to Toshio.
Dialogue: 0,1:17:49.80,1:17:53.92,Default,,0,0,0,,Given their relationship,
Dialogue: 0,1:17:54.22,1:17:56.51,Default,,0,0,0,,It’s difficult to believe that...
Dialogue: 0,1:17:56.55,1:18:01.27,Default,,0,0,0,,Koyuki would really kill Toshio,\Nas the note said.
Dialogue: 0,1:18:01.47,1:18:02.93,Default,,0,0,0,,So who could’ve killed him?
Dialogue: 0,1:18:04.48,1:18:08.98,Default,,0,0,0,,Someone else had to have been there.
Dialogue: 0,1:18:10.61,1:18:12.99,Default,,0,0,0,,Here’s your egg and rice.
Dialogue: 0,1:18:13.44,1:18:15.74,Default,,0,0,0,,- Eat up.\N- Don’t mind if I do.
Dialogue: 0,1:18:16.86,1:18:21.99,Default,,0,0,0,,Do you think that a young girl is capable\Nof chopping off a man’s head...
Dialogue: 0,1:18:22.12,1:18:24.83,Default,,0,0,0,,and stringing it from a chandelier?
Dialogue: 0,1:18:25.04,1:18:28.33,Default,,0,0,0,,She would've also had to drag\Nthe headless body off somewhere.
Dialogue: 0,1:18:28.58,1:18:32.13,Default,,0,0,0,,Like the mother with her child\Ntrapped under a car,
Dialogue: 0,1:18:33.01,1:18:37.43,Default,,0,0,0,,people are capable of all kinds of things\Nwhen they’re in a bind.
Dialogue: 0,1:18:37.68,1:18:39.60,Default,,0,0,0,,I don’t think so.
Dialogue: 0,1:18:41.93,1:18:44.68,Default,,0,0,0,,How are {\i1}The Angry Pirates{\i0}?
Dialogue: 0,1:18:44.93,1:18:50.15,Default,,0,0,0,,I've been watching them like a hawk,\Nbut I think they're leaving town.
Dialogue: 0,1:18:50.31,1:18:52.19,Default,,0,0,0,,That’s what three of them said\Nwhen I talked to them just now.
Dialogue: 0,1:18:52.32,1:18:54.53,Default,,0,0,0,,Wait a minute, I thought there were\Nstill four members left.
Dialogue: 0,1:18:54.57,1:18:57.78,Default,,0,0,0,,Yoshizawa wasn’t there.\NThere was a phone call from a girl.
Dialogue: 0,1:18:58.03,1:19:00.57,Default,,0,0,0,,He went to the empty garage that\NToshio had been staying at, or something.
Dialogue: 0,1:19:00.78,1:19:03.83,Default,,0,0,0,,When did you learn of this?
Dialogue: 0,1:19:35.40,1:19:38.36,Default,,0,0,0,,What!? Again!?
Dialogue: 0,1:19:38.82,1:19:42.24,Default,,0,0,0,,This makes three!
Dialogue: 0,1:19:42.95,1:19:45.24,Default,,0,0,0,,Don’t apologize, you dolt!
Dialogue: 0,1:19:45.45,1:19:47.08,Default,,0,0,0,,Where did it happen?
Dialogue: 0,1:19:48.66,1:19:50.50,Default,,0,0,0,,The same garage?!
Dialogue: 0,1:19:50.96,1:19:53.25,Default,,0,0,0,,He couldn’t hurt a fly!
Dialogue: 0,1:19:53.88,1:19:56.13,Default,,0,0,0,,Let me see him!
Dialogue: 0,1:19:56.42,1:20:01.51,Default,,0,0,0,,I will, I will. Please calm down.\NHe’s being held as a suspect.
Dialogue: 0,1:20:01.55,1:20:06.35,Default,,0,0,0,,Shigeru left the house after receiving\Na phone call at 4:30pm, is that correct?
Dialogue: 0,1:20:06.43,1:20:08.64,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes, he wouldn’t lie.
Dialogue: 0,1:20:08.85,1:20:12.06,Default,,0,0,0,,And he told you that he was going\Nto the garage?
Dialogue: 0,1:20:12.31,1:20:13.86,Default,,0,0,0,,I didn’t ask where he was going.
Dialogue: 0,1:20:14.15,1:20:17.69,Default,,0,0,0,,Bando, didn’t {\i1}The Angry Pirates{\i0} say that...
Dialogue: 0,1:20:18.07,1:20:23.20,Default,,0,0,0,,- Yoshizawa left to meet Shigeru?\N- Yes.
Dialogue: 0,1:20:23.62,1:20:27.74,Default,,0,0,0,,- Did they say why?\N- He apparently didn’t say.
Dialogue: 0,1:20:27.95,1:20:32.00,Default,,0,0,0,,But they did say that Yoshizawa had met\NShigeru on two or three other occasions.
Dialogue: 0,1:20:32.21,1:20:35.54,Default,,0,0,0,,I see...\NI got it!
Dialogue: 0,1:20:35.79,1:20:38.38,Default,,0,0,0,,Shigeru perpetrated the crime.
Dialogue: 0,1:20:38.59,1:20:41.84,Default,,0,0,0,,How dare you!
Dialogue: 0,1:20:45.51,1:20:47.81,Default,,0,0,0,,Stop your weeping!
Dialogue: 0,1:20:49.56,1:20:53.40,Default,,0,0,0,,Your son was found at the site\Nof the murder.
Dialogue: 0,1:20:53.44,1:20:57.65,Default,,0,0,0,,All the evidence points to him as\Nthe killer. This is what happened:
Dialogue: 0,1:20:57.69,1:21:01.40,Default,,0,0,0,,Yoshizawa telephoned Shigeru\Nto meet him.
Dialogue: 0,1:21:01.61,1:21:04.70,Default,,0,0,0,,Yoshizawa threatened Shigeru\Nat the garage.
Dialogue: 0,1:21:04.74,1:21:08.49,Default,,0,0,0,,Unable to comply with\NYoshizawa’s demands,
Dialogue: 0,1:21:08.70,1:21:11.83,Default,,0,0,0,,Shigeru lost his wits and killed\NYoshizawa with his own guitar.
Dialogue: 0,1:21:12.04,1:21:13.83,Default,,0,0,0,,What did Yoshizawa threaten to do?
Dialogue: 0,1:21:13.87,1:21:16.84,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, yeah. Let me see…
Dialogue: 0,1:21:17.88,1:21:23.34,Default,,0,0,0,,Yoshizawa was going to accuse Yukari Hogen\Nof actually being Koyuki Yamauchi.
Dialogue: 0,1:21:24.38,1:21:25.76,Default,,0,0,0,,So Shigeru…
Dialogue: 0,1:21:26.01,1:21:29.26,Default,,0,0,0,,What are you gibbering on about?
Dialogue: 0,1:21:29.47,1:21:34.23,Default,,0,0,0,,That girl {\i1}is{\i0} Yukari. Both the mother and\Nthe girl herself confirmed this.
Dialogue: 0,1:21:35.69,1:21:37.90,Default,,0,0,0,,The threat was related to\NYoshizawa’s livelihood.
Dialogue: 0,1:21:37.94,1:21:43.24,Default,,0,0,0,,Two members of {\i1}The Angry Pirates{\i0}\Nwere gone because of the Hogen family,
Dialogue: 0,1:21:43.45,1:21:46.66,Default,,0,0,0,,and this compromised\Ntheir ability to make money.
Dialogue: 0,1:21:46.82,1:21:50.74,Default,,0,0,0,,Yoshizawa wanted compensation\Nfor this from Shigeru.
Dialogue: 0,1:21:50.95,1:21:57.83,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}People will go to great lengths\Nto survive in this world.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:22:08.63,1:22:10.63,Default,,0,0,0,,I screwed up again.
Dialogue: 0,1:22:11.21,1:22:15.22,Default,,0,0,0,,No, I think you were actually correct.
Dialogue: 0,1:22:16.89,1:22:21.10,Default,,0,0,0,,Yoshizawa did think that\NYukari was Koyuki.
Dialogue: 0,1:22:23.85,1:22:26.73,Default,,0,0,0,,I think Shigeru was framed.
Dialogue: 0,1:22:28.82,1:22:31.15,Default,,0,0,0,,That would make the real killer\Nquite formidable.
Dialogue: 0,1:22:33.74,1:22:35.78,Default,,0,0,0,,I feel bad for the real killer.
Dialogue: 0,1:22:36.11,1:22:39.91,Default,,0,0,0,,Kindaichi, you seem to identify\Nwith criminals.
Dialogue: 0,1:22:41.08,1:22:43.00,Default,,0,0,0,,Are you always like this?
Dialogue: 0,1:22:43.20,1:22:47.79,Default,,0,0,0,,By this time of the year, my home town\Nis surely blanketed in snow.
Dialogue: 0,1:22:48.63,1:22:51.42,Default,,0,0,0,,Are you from Tohoku?
Dialogue: 0,1:22:51.88,1:22:53.47,Default,,0,0,0,,My family was poor.
Dialogue: 0,1:22:54.55,1:22:57.30,Default,,0,0,0,,I went to the US to work\Nas a dishwasher.
Dialogue: 0,1:22:59.30,1:23:02.93,Default,,0,0,0,,I was separated from my parents\Nwhen I was still small.
Dialogue: 0,1:23:03.56,1:23:06.52,Default,,0,0,0,,Just like me.
Dialogue: 0,1:23:08.23,1:23:13.69,Default,,0,0,0,,I get the feeling that the criminal\Nin this case is a lot like me.
Dialogue: 0,1:23:15.95,1:23:17.74,Default,,0,0,0,,Mokutaro.
Dialogue: 0,1:23:17.91,1:23:23.08,Default,,0,0,0,,- I’m going to southern Tohoku.\N- Why?
Dialogue: 0,1:23:23.12,1:23:26.54,Default,,0,0,0,,I want to look into wind chimes\Nproduced there.
Dialogue: 0,1:23:26.75,1:23:29.58,Default,,0,0,0,,I think it holds the key to\Ncracking this case.
Dialogue: 0,1:23:29.79,1:23:33.13,Default,,0,0,0,,- When are you going?\N- As soon as possible.
Dialogue: 0,1:23:33.38,1:23:37.63,Default,,0,0,0,,There’s something I want you\Nto do while I’m gone.
Dialogue: 0,1:23:37.80,1:23:39.34,Default,,0,0,0,,What is it?
Dialogue: 0,1:23:40.64,1:23:44.27,Default,,0,0,0,,Don’t worry, I can take care\Nof anything you want.
Dialogue: 0,1:23:55.28,1:23:58.82,Default,,0,0,0,,- Are you all right?\N- Don’t worry.
Dialogue: 0,1:23:58.95,1:24:03.03,Default,,0,0,0,,I heard that after Sannosuke spoke\Non the phone for you,
Dialogue: 0,1:24:03.24,1:24:06.29,Default,,0,0,0,,you immediately took to your bed.
Dialogue: 0,1:24:06.50,1:24:08.46,Default,,0,0,0,,Who called?
Dialogue: 0,1:24:08.71,1:24:11.46,Default,,0,0,0,,It’s nothing for you to worry about.
Dialogue: 0,1:24:12.54,1:24:14.59,Default,,0,0,0,,I want to know.
Dialogue: 0,1:24:17.09,1:24:19.22,Default,,0,0,0,,Tokubei was murdered.
Dialogue: 0,1:24:21.89,1:24:23.60,Default,,0,0,0,,Yoshizawa, too.
Dialogue: 0,1:24:24.51,1:24:27.10,Default,,0,0,0,,Shigeru is still under arrest.
Dialogue: 0,1:24:27.48,1:24:29.73,Default,,0,0,0,,The whole thing ties back to me.
Dialogue: 0,1:24:30.44,1:24:32.56,Default,,0,0,0,,I’m handling it.
Dialogue: 0,1:24:32.94,1:24:37.32,Default,,0,0,0,,Yoshizawa knew that you were Koyuki.
Dialogue: 0,1:24:37.61,1:24:42.53,Default,,0,0,0,,When Yoshizawa called your name\Nin town was anyone around?
Dialogue: 0,1:24:42.78,1:24:44.91,Default,,0,0,0,,I don’t know.
Dialogue: 0,1:24:46.87,1:24:52.50,Default,,0,0,0,,Someone might know and could\Nbe planning something.
Dialogue: 0,1:25:03.89,1:25:05.14,Default,,0,0,0,,What’s this?
Dialogue: 0,1:25:05.89,1:25:07.72,Default,,0,0,0,,My mother gave it to me.
Dialogue: 0,1:25:10.69,1:25:17.44,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Fuyuko,\Nborn December 17, 1913,\NJinzaburo{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:25:21.20,1:25:23.41,Default,,0,0,0,,I never imagined!
Dialogue: 0,1:25:25.45,1:25:29.66,Default,,0,0,0,,The reason that Fuyuko came\Nto visit was….
Dialogue: 0,1:25:34.00,1:25:35.88,Default,,0,0,0,,Fuyuko!
Dialogue: 0,1:25:38.63,1:25:41.42,Default,,0,0,0,,- What did I do?!\N- Leave me alone!
Dialogue: 0,1:25:51.77,1:25:58.23,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Mizusawa City,\NIwate Prefecture{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:26:29.06,1:26:34.56,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Kitakami City,\NIwate Prefecture{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:27:17.48,1:27:19.11,Default,,0,0,0,,There you go.
Dialogue: 0,1:27:20.36,1:27:24.07,Default,,0,0,0,,All of this is on Fuyuko Yamauchi?
Dialogue: 0,1:27:24.28,1:27:25.74,Default,,0,0,0,,Of course not.
Dialogue: 0,1:27:25.90,1:27:29.87,Default,,0,0,0,,A lot of it I just took out because it\Nbrings back memories.
Dialogue: 0,1:27:30.16,1:27:31.95,Default,,0,0,0,,Here, take a look at this.
Dialogue: 0,1:27:32.16,1:27:37.92,Default,,0,0,0,,The sergeant insisted that\Nit was an accident,
Dialogue: 0,1:27:38.00,1:27:42.09,Default,,0,0,0,,but I suspected that it was suicide.\NI turned out to be right.
Dialogue: 0,1:27:42.30,1:27:46.63,Default,,0,0,0,,Do you remember the 13-member household\Nthat committed suicide together?
Dialogue: 0,1:27:46.80,1:27:50.18,Default,,0,0,0,,- No.\N- You don’t?
Dialogue: 0,1:27:52.72,1:27:58.81,Default,,0,0,0,,I was always the detective stuck\Ninvestigating suicides.
Dialogue: 0,1:28:00.40,1:28:02.98,Default,,0,0,0,,Here it is: Fuyuko Yamauchi.
Dialogue: 0,1:28:03.82,1:28:05.86,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, yeah, you’re right.
Dialogue: 0,1:28:06.07,1:28:11.20,Default,,0,0,0,,Mr. Kindaichi wanted me\Nto confirm that...
Dialogue: 0,1:28:11.45,1:28:16.79,Default,,0,0,0,,she had a mole on the\Nright side of her chin.
Dialogue: 0,1:28:16.91,1:28:18.00,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes.
Dialogue: 0,1:28:19.37,1:28:24.71,Default,,0,0,0,,I don’t remember it.
Dialogue: 0,1:28:26.13,1:28:28.97,Default,,0,0,0,,What’s your connection\Nwith Mr. Kindaichi?
Dialogue: 0,1:28:29.18,1:28:31.39,Default,,0,0,0,,He asked me to check on this.
Dialogue: 0,1:28:31.97,1:28:35.27,Default,,0,0,0,,Do you like being a PI’s assistant?
Dialogue: 0,1:28:35.47,1:28:37.48,Default,,0,0,0,,It’s a tough job.
Dialogue: 0,1:28:37.52,1:28:41.77,Default,,0,0,0,,Do you plan to be a private eye\Nyourself someday?
Dialogue: 0,1:28:42.11,1:28:45.61,Default,,0,0,0,,No, I’m not like him.
Dialogue: 0,1:28:47.24,1:28:51.20,Default,,0,0,0,,Look here!\NFuyuko Yamauchi.
Dialogue: 0,1:28:52.32,1:28:55.24,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, we found it!
Dialogue: 0,1:28:55.29,1:28:57.08,Default,,0,0,0,,Are you going to write this down?
Dialogue: 0,1:28:59.58,1:29:04.50,Default,,0,0,0,,She had a mole around 2cm below\Nher lip on the right side,
Dialogue: 0,1:29:04.71,1:29:08.09,Default,,0,0,0,,about the size of a large grain of rice.
Dialogue: 0,1:29:10.13,1:29:12.26,Default,,0,0,0,,This is my handwriting!
Dialogue: 0,1:29:13.05,1:29:17.81,Default,,0,0,0,,I was able to carry on because\NI had Shigeru.
Dialogue: 0,1:29:18.93,1:29:23.56,Default,,0,0,0,,Otherwise, I would have\Nno reason to live.
Dialogue: 0,1:29:23.69,1:29:28.36,Default,,0,0,0,,Every piece of evidence that we have points\Nto your son as the criminal.
Dialogue: 0,1:29:29.03,1:29:31.74,Default,,0,0,0,,- He's right. - We ask for your patience\Nfor the time being.
Dialogue: 0,1:29:31.99,1:29:33.57,Default,,0,0,0,,If you were a mother,\Nyou’d understand!
Dialogue: 0,1:29:33.87,1:29:35.95,Default,,0,0,0,,Imbecile, don’t be so callous!
Dialogue: 0,1:29:40.79,1:29:43.50,Default,,0,0,0,,Mrs. Tanabe, just the woman\NI wanted to see.
Dialogue: 0,1:29:43.88,1:29:45.79,Default,,0,0,0,,There’s something I need to ask.
Dialogue: 0,1:29:46.00,1:29:48.88,Default,,0,0,0,,- What are you doing here?\N- Mr. Kindaichi asked me to.
Dialogue: 0,1:29:48.88,1:29:52.76,Default,,0,0,0,,- The flatfoot? - This is crucial to\Nclearing up all three of the murders.
Dialogue: 0,1:29:53.30,1:29:57.31,Default,,0,0,0,,Big talk! Where is that guy anyhow?
Dialogue: 0,1:29:57.35,1:29:59.56,Default,,0,0,0,,The morning after Toshio’s head\Nwas discovered,
Dialogue: 0,1:29:59.77,1:30:02.23,Default,,0,0,0,,I saw Yukari at the abandoned\NHogen house.
Dialogue: 0,1:30:02.56,1:30:06.90,Default,,0,0,0,,You and Shigeru had a suspicious\Nlook on your faces. Why?
Dialogue: 0,1:30:07.19,1:30:11.36,Default,,0,0,0,,We didn’t know that Yukari\Nhad returned home.
Dialogue: 0,1:30:15.03,1:30:16.74,Default,,0,0,0,,Where had she been?
Dialogue: 0,1:30:16.95,1:30:18.87,Default,,0,0,0,,The lodge on Mount Hiei.\NShe didn’t say where she was going.
Dialogue: 0,1:30:18.99,1:30:20.83,Default,,0,0,0,,- How many days was she gone?\N- Three.
Dialogue: 0,1:30:21.00,1:30:23.25,Default,,0,0,0,,What are you getting at?
Dialogue: 0,1:30:23.33,1:30:28.46,Default,,0,0,0,,Inspector, {\i1}The Angry Pirates{\i0} came to town\Nthree days before the murder.
Dialogue: 0,1:30:28.75,1:30:32.09,Default,,0,0,0,,The same number of days that\NYukari was out of town.
Dialogue: 0,1:30:34.09,1:30:38.56,Default,,0,0,0,,Why didn’t you tell us this before?
Dialogue: 0,1:30:38.85,1:30:42.27,Default,,0,0,0,,Yayoi told me to keep it a secret.
Dialogue: 0,1:30:42.81,1:30:44.27,Default,,0,0,0,,Why?
Dialogue: 0,1:31:45.54,1:31:47.54,Default,,0,0,0,,How are you feeling?
Dialogue: 0,1:31:50.04,1:31:51.92,Default,,0,0,0,,I’m such a burden.
Dialogue: 0,1:31:52.38,1:31:54.63,Default,,0,0,0,,Mother, not again.
Dialogue: 0,1:31:55.55,1:31:58.97,Default,,0,0,0,,That was a long time ago.
Dialogue: 0,1:32:12.40,1:32:14.57,Default,,0,0,0,,Uncle Mozo.
Dialogue: 0,1:32:14.82,1:32:19.66,Default,,0,0,0,,- Please be nice to mommy.\N- Yayoi.
Dialogue: 0,1:32:23.08,1:32:25.41,Default,,0,0,0,,I was wrong...
Dialogue: 0,1:32:25.45,1:32:31.21,Default,,0,0,0,,to send you from the Hogen family\Nto be an Igarashi.
Dialogue: 0,1:32:31.42,1:32:33.96,Default,,0,0,0,,I told you to forget about that.
Dialogue: 0,1:32:34.55,1:32:37.13,Default,,0,0,0,,I don’t care anymore.
Dialogue: 0,1:32:53.69,1:32:57.82,Default,,0,0,0,,Father, I’ve promised a gentleman\Nthat I would marry him.
Dialogue: 0,1:32:57.94,1:32:59.28,Default,,0,0,0,,I know.
Dialogue: 0,1:32:59.32,1:33:05.49,Default,,0,0,0,,I can’t marry my cousin\NTakuya Hogen.
Dialogue: 0,1:33:06.45,1:33:08.25,Default,,0,0,0,,You…
Dialogue: 0,1:33:08.41,1:33:12.46,Default,,0,0,0,,You think that you can use it\Nto control me.
Dialogue: 0,1:33:12.83,1:33:16.21,Default,,0,0,0,,Please forgive her, Mozo.
Dialogue: 0,1:33:16.42,1:33:19.67,Default,,0,0,0,,Women are happiest when they're\Nprotected by a man.
Dialogue: 0,1:33:19.88,1:33:22.89,Default,,0,0,0,,- Leave this decision to me.\N- I won’t!
Dialogue: 0,1:33:22.97,1:33:25.06,Default,,0,0,0,,You’re not going to change my mind.
Dialogue: 0,1:33:25.56,1:33:27.14,Default,,0,0,0,,Please!
Dialogue: 0,1:33:29.27,1:33:35.44,Default,,0,0,0,,I said, no!\NYou best mind me, woman!
Dialogue: 0,1:33:43.20,1:33:47.83,Default,,0,0,0,,I'll never forget that day.
Dialogue: 0,1:33:50.25,1:33:55.63,Default,,0,0,0,,It was an accident.\NThat’s all.
Dialogue: 0,1:33:55.79,1:33:59.80,Default,,0,0,0,,Nobody knows about it.
Dialogue: 0,1:34:00.30,1:34:04.09,Default,,0,0,0,,I’ve become such a burden to you.
Dialogue: 0,1:34:04.68,1:34:08.81,Default,,0,0,0,,Everything is for the house of Hogen.
Dialogue: 0,1:34:13.94,1:34:18.27,Default,,0,0,0,,Mr. Kindaichi,\NNaokichi’s been severely injured.
Dialogue: 0,1:34:20.19,1:34:21.90,Default,,0,0,0,,Did you come straight from\Nthe train station?
Dialogue: 0,1:34:21.95,1:34:25.95,Default,,0,0,0,,I was surprised. Thanks for calling.\NHow is he?
Dialogue: 0,1:34:26.62,1:34:28.66,Default,,0,0,0,,He’s still in a coma.
Dialogue: 0,1:34:28.70,1:34:33.08,Default,,0,0,0,,I really screwed the pooch this time.\NYou trusted me.
Dialogue: 0,1:34:34.04,1:34:39.17,Default,,0,0,0,,Red… lamp...
Dialogue: 0,1:34:46.30,1:34:49.39,Default,,0,0,0,,He mumbled something.
Dialogue: 0,1:34:51.35,1:34:55.98,Default,,0,0,0,,When they brought him in he said,\N"Red lamp." He kept repeating it.
Dialogue: 0,1:34:58.73,1:35:00.15,Default,,0,0,0,,"Red lamp"?
Dialogue: 0,1:35:26.26,1:35:28.30,Default,,0,0,0,,I’m Mr. Kindaichi.
Dialogue: 0,1:35:28.76,1:35:31.43,Default,,0,0,0,,Isn’t this Toshio Yamauchi’s grave?
Dialogue: 0,1:35:36.27,1:35:40.86,Default,,0,0,0,,Toshio didn’t have any relatives,\Nso Yayoi claimed his body...
Dialogue: 0,1:35:41.11,1:35:44.57,Default,,0,0,0,,and gave him a proper funeral.\NI heard it from the police.
Dialogue: 0,1:35:47.95,1:35:52.83,Default,,0,0,0,,I can’t think of any reason that Yukari\Nwould have for visiting Toshio’s gravesite.
Dialogue: 0,1:35:54.37,1:35:57.42,Default,,0,0,0,,You’re Koyuki Yamauchi, aren’t you?
Dialogue: 0,1:35:59.58,1:36:03.63,Default,,0,0,0,,I don’t think that bogus suicide note\Nwas your idea.
Dialogue: 0,1:36:03.71,1:36:06.38,Default,,0,0,0,,- It wasn’t all a lie!\N- You’re withholding vital information.
Dialogue: 0,1:36:06.55,1:36:08.55,Default,,0,0,0,,I’d imagine you’d want to learn\Nthe truth as well.
Dialogue: 0,1:36:08.76,1:36:11.64,Default,,0,0,0,,Please tell me what happened.
Dialogue: 0,1:36:29.99,1:36:33.37,Default,,0,0,0,,There were signs that the piece\Nholding the chandelier...
Dialogue: 0,1:36:33.70,1:36:38.87,Default,,0,0,0,,in place at the House of Hanging\Nhad been rigged to fall easily.
Dialogue: 0,1:36:39.67,1:36:41.75,Default,,0,0,0,,So this was planned?
Dialogue: 0,1:36:42.21,1:36:44.38,Default,,0,0,0,,How is Naokichi doing?
Dialogue: 0,1:36:44.63,1:36:47.13,Default,,0,0,0,,Apparently, he’s going to live.
Dialogue: 0,1:36:48.51,1:36:50.55,Default,,0,0,0,,Mr. Kindaichi asks that you come\Nto the Hogen house immediately.
Dialogue: 0,1:36:50.76,1:36:52.18,Default,,0,0,0,,He wants to explain the details\Nof the case.
Dialogue: 0,1:36:52.39,1:36:55.68,Default,,0,0,0,,I have better things to do, and I don’t\Nmuch care to be ordered around by that two-bit PI.
Dialogue: 0,1:36:55.89,1:36:57.64,Default,,0,0,0,,I’m not going.
Dialogue: 0,1:36:57.85,1:37:01.15,Default,,0,0,0,,- Yukari is actually Koyuki!\N- What?!
Dialogue: 0,1:37:01.35,1:37:03.65,Default,,0,0,0,,She said so herself.
Dialogue: 0,1:37:05.65,1:37:08.95,Default,,0,0,0,,If that’s true,\Nthen Yukari is missing.
Dialogue: 0,1:37:09.15,1:37:10.45,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, yeah.
Dialogue: 0,1:37:10.61,1:37:13.95,Default,,0,0,0,,We can’t rule out the possibility that\NYukari is the perpetrator.
Dialogue: 0,1:37:14.20,1:37:18.20,Default,,0,0,0,,I wonder why Yayoi's protecting her.
Dialogue: 0,1:37:18.25,1:37:20.75,Default,,0,0,0,,- It’s her daughter.\N- I know that.
Dialogue: 0,1:37:20.79,1:37:22.58,Default,,0,0,0,,- You’re wrong.\N- Why?
Dialogue: 0,1:37:22.79,1:37:25.67,Default,,0,0,0,,- It’s a little more complicated than that.\N- What are you talking about?
Dialogue: 0,1:37:25.88,1:37:28.13,Default,,0,0,0,,- I’m telling you that you don’t\Nunderstand. - That hurts.
Dialogue: 0,1:37:28.38,1:37:32.14,Default,,0,0,0,,Quit that insufferable prattle!\NWe have to go to the Hogen house.
Dialogue: 0,1:37:42.44,1:37:45.65,Default,,0,0,0,,How long have you been here?
Dialogue: 0,1:37:46.69,1:37:50.15,Default,,0,0,0,,No one was here,\Nso I let myself in.
Dialogue: 0,1:37:53.11,1:37:54.91,Default,,0,0,0,,What do you want?
Dialogue: 0,1:37:55.24,1:37:59.54,Default,,0,0,0,,I’ve been to southern Tohoku.
Dialogue: 0,1:38:00.41,1:38:06.38,Default,,0,0,0,,After Toshio’s head was found dangling\Nfrom the ceiling, Tokubei was killed,
Dialogue: 0,1:38:06.59,1:38:10.22,Default,,0,0,0,,Yoshizawa was killed.\NIt constitutes a string of murders.
Dialogue: 0,1:38:10.42,1:38:13.59,Default,,0,0,0,,Although there is no obvious link\Nbetween these three cases,
Dialogue: 0,1:38:13.80,1:38:16.81,Default,,0,0,0,,they all have a common root.
Dialogue: 0,1:38:17.01,1:38:21.94,Default,,0,0,0,,Mr. Kindaichi, I hope you remember\Nthat I hired you to find Koyuki.
Dialogue: 0,1:38:22.10,1:38:23.94,Default,,0,0,0,,That’s also significant.
Dialogue: 0,1:38:24.48,1:38:28.82,Default,,0,0,0,,Yayoi, there’s someone living in\Nyour attic, isn’t there?
Dialogue: 0,1:38:30.36,1:38:33.03,Default,,0,0,0,,Why are you keeping it a secret?
Dialogue: 0,1:38:36.07,1:38:37.62,Default,,0,0,0,,Isn’t it Chizu?
Dialogue: 0,1:38:38.03,1:38:43.00,Default,,0,0,0,,Is there anything suspicious about\Ntaking care of my mother as I see fit?
Dialogue: 0,1:38:49.80,1:38:53.05,Default,,0,0,0,,When I went to southern Tohoku,
Dialogue: 0,1:38:53.22,1:38:57.47,Default,,0,0,0,,it was because I came into possession\Nof this songbook.
Dialogue: 0,1:38:57.80,1:39:00.35,Default,,0,0,0,,You never read it, right?
Dialogue: 0,1:39:00.39,1:39:03.64,Default,,0,0,0,,I already told you that.
Dialogue: 0,1:39:04.73,1:39:08.65,Default,,0,0,0,,"I visited the town of\NKawaaoki Kitakami,
Dialogue: 0,1:39:08.69,1:39:12.32,Default,,0,0,0,,"and didn’t tell my mother,\Nfrom mistrust of days past."
Dialogue: 0,1:39:12.57,1:39:15.86,Default,,0,0,0,,It’s a part of a song your husband\NTakuya wrote.
Dialogue: 0,1:39:17.03,1:39:21.75,Default,,0,0,0,,Takuya was a secret bastard son of\Nthe first generation of Hogens,
Dialogue: 0,1:39:21.75,1:39:24.87,Default,,0,0,0,,- Tetsuma Hogen, right?\N- How did you know that?
Dialogue: 0,1:39:24.91,1:39:27.79,Default,,0,0,0,,Takuma’s wife died young.\NHe didn’t have an heir,
Dialogue: 0,1:39:27.79,1:39:32.13,Default,,0,0,0,,so he wanted to make Takuya\Nthe official heir to the Hogen Hospital.
Dialogue: 0,1:39:32.17,1:39:35.43,Default,,0,0,0,,but the Hogen family was quite prominent,\Nand the moral climate...
Dialogue: 0,1:39:35.68,1:39:38.72,Default,,0,0,0,,wouldn’t tolerate making\Na courtesan’s child the official heir.
Dialogue: 0,1:39:38.93,1:39:44.23,Default,,0,0,0,,But Mozo Igarashi didn’t let that\Nget in his way.
Dialogue: 0,1:39:45.60,1:39:50.65,Default,,0,0,0,,Mozo took Takuya from his mother,\Nkicked her off this land,
Dialogue: 0,1:39:50.82,1:39:54.07,Default,,0,0,0,,and turned the neighborhood\Nagainst her.
Dialogue: 0,1:39:55.53,1:40:01.28,Default,,0,0,0,,Takuya wrote this song when\Nhe visited Kitami years later,
Dialogue: 0,1:40:01.45,1:40:05.91,Default,,0,0,0,,and was stricken by grief over\Nhis banished mother.
Dialogue: 0,1:40:08.71,1:40:12.42,Default,,0,0,0,,Her name was Sumi Miyasaka.
Dialogue: 0,1:40:12.46,1:40:16.05,Default,,0,0,0,,I know, I met her!
Dialogue: 0,1:40:16.09,1:40:19.76,Default,,0,0,0,,What?! I heard she died.
Dialogue: 0,1:40:20.93,1:40:26.69,Default,,0,0,0,,Sumi kept a low profile out of\Nconsideration for her son Takuya.
Dialogue: 0,1:40:26.89,1:40:30.27,Default,,0,0,0,,She moved around a lot,
Dialogue: 0,1:40:30.48,1:40:34.98,Default,,0,0,0,,but I found her name in an old ledger\Nat the Kitakami city hall.
Dialogue: 0,1:40:35.65,1:40:41.03,Default,,0,0,0,,I bet I wasn’t easy to find.
Dialogue: 0,1:40:41.24,1:40:46.12,Default,,0,0,0,,I’ve had several husbands.
Dialogue: 0,1:40:46.50,1:40:52.13,Default,,0,0,0,,Mozo Igarashi was also from\Nsouthern Tohoku.
Dialogue: 0,1:40:53.09,1:40:57.92,Default,,0,0,0,,The Hogen family owes...
Dialogue: 0,1:40:57.97,1:41:06.06,Default,,0,0,0,,a great debt to me for Takuya.
Dialogue: 0,1:41:06.68,1:41:10.48,Default,,0,0,0,,Chizu was the younger...
Dialogue: 0,1:41:10.77,1:41:19.28,Default,,0,0,0,,half-sister of Tetsuma\Nby different mothers.
Dialogue: 0,1:41:19.74,1:41:27.29,Default,,0,0,0,,They fell in love,\Nbut it would have been incest to marry.
Dialogue: 0,1:41:27.45,1:41:31.08,Default,,0,0,0,,They had a bastard child, Yayoi.
Dialogue: 0,1:41:31.46,1:41:38.01,Default,,0,0,0,,Mozo wanted Chizu for his wife.
Dialogue: 0,1:41:38.21,1:41:45.97,Default,,0,0,0,,He begged Tetsuma to permit\Nthe marriage.
Dialogue: 0,1:41:46.81,1:41:51.90,Default,,0,0,0,,It was a tough time for a woman\Nto raise a child by herself.
Dialogue: 0,1:41:52.98,1:41:58.23,Default,,0,0,0,,And the decision of\Nthe {\i1}paterfamilias{\i0} was final.
Dialogue: 0,1:41:58.53,1:42:04.49,Default,,0,0,0,,My mother was like a puppet.
Dialogue: 0,1:42:04.62,1:42:13.38,Default,,0,0,0,,I was shocked when I heard that\NYayoi had married Takuya.
Dialogue: 0,1:42:14.00,1:42:19.42,Default,,0,0,0,,They were cousins, after all.
Dialogue: 0,1:42:19.63,1:42:24.97,Default,,0,0,0,,but their marriage made Mozo...
Dialogue: 0,1:42:24.97,1:42:33.27,Default,,0,0,0,,a closer member of the Hogen family,
Dialogue: 0,1:42:33.52,1:42:41.65,Default,,0,0,0,,and no doubt he wanted to run\Nthe Hogen Hospital.
Dialogue: 0,1:42:42.11,1:42:52.21,Default,,0,0,0,,Mozo’s unrelenting ambition was\Nsometimes fearsome.
Dialogue: 0,1:42:53.75,1:42:59.50,Default,,0,0,0,,What kind of couple do you think\NTakuya and Yayoi made?
Dialogue: 0,1:43:00.30,1:43:05.76,Default,,0,0,0,,Of course, I stopped being a mother\Nto Takuya a long time ago,
Dialogue: 0,1:43:05.97,1:43:10.31,Default,,0,0,0,,so I suppose it doesn’t matter\Nto me anymore. What?
Dialogue: 0,1:43:10.56,1:43:14.98,Default,,0,0,0,,There’s something written\Nabout me in the book.
Dialogue: 0,1:43:17.06,1:43:22.15,Default,,0,0,0,,I’m sorry, but I can’t see well.
Dialogue: 0,1:43:22.15,1:43:25.24,Default,,0,0,0,,Actually, I’m illiterate.
Dialogue: 0,1:43:25.45,1:43:28.07,Default,,0,0,0,,I can’t read.
Dialogue: 0,1:43:30.08,1:43:38.42,Default,,0,0,0,,I had no idea that Mozo Igarashi\Nwas such a menace to you.
Dialogue: 0,1:43:38.67,1:43:41.30,Default,,0,0,0,,- He died a long time ago.\N- You’re wrong.
Dialogue: 0,1:43:41.46,1:43:44.22,Default,,0,0,0,,You haven’t rid yourself of him.
Dialogue: 0,1:43:45.59,1:43:50.85,Default,,0,0,0,,I found a photograph.
Dialogue: 0,1:43:51.35,1:43:53.27,Default,,0,0,0,,I've no idea what you’re talking about.
Dialogue: 0,1:43:53.48,1:43:57.23,Default,,0,0,0,,The murders were all connected\Nto that photo.
Dialogue: 0,1:43:59.52,1:44:02.69,Default,,0,0,0,,The murderer… is you.
Dialogue: 0,1:44:08.16,1:44:10.45,Default,,0,0,0,,I have the photo.
Dialogue: 0,1:44:24.71,1:44:29.39,Default,,0,0,0,,The dry plate for the photo is inside.
Dialogue: 0,1:44:36.18,1:44:41.23,Default,,0,0,0,,You saw it?
Dialogue: 0,1:44:44.28,1:44:45.82,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes.
Dialogue: 0,1:44:59.75,1:45:02.92,Default,,0,0,0,,Honjo, hurry up and take the photo!
Dialogue: 0,1:45:20.94,1:45:28.57,Default,,0,0,0,,I’m the only one who’s seen\Nthe photo.
Dialogue: 0,1:45:30.78,1:45:33.78,Default,,0,0,0,,An attached piece of paper dates\Nthe dry plate to January 1, 1913,
Dialogue: 0,1:45:33.99,1:45:36.95,Default,,0,0,0,,and identifies Monjuro Honjo\Nas the photographer.
Dialogue: 0,1:45:37.25,1:45:43.08,Default,,0,0,0,,That would’ve have made you 15 years old,\Nwhich is before you married Takuya.
Dialogue: 0,1:45:43.34,1:45:47.05,Default,,0,0,0,,You got pregnant and gave birth\Nto a girl that winter.
Dialogue: 0,1:45:47.09,1:45:49.76,Default,,0,0,0,,That was Fuyuko, and she hanged herself\Nin the House of Hanging.
Dialogue: 0,1:45:49.92,1:45:51.26,Default,,0,0,0,,How do you know this?
Dialogue: 0,1:45:53.22,1:45:57.27,Default,,0,0,0,,I would’ve thought you’d have\Nfigured that out by now.
Dialogue: 0,1:45:58.22,1:46:03.36,Default,,0,0,0,,Koyuki told me when she picked up\NFuyuko’s wind chime.
Dialogue: 0,1:46:04.69,1:46:10.95,Default,,0,0,0,,She didn’t seem to know anything\Nabout it.
Dialogue: 0,1:46:15.53,1:46:24.25,Default,,0,0,0,,The truth was too awful to tell Koyuki.
Dialogue: 0,1:46:25.25,1:46:28.96,Default,,0,0,0,,There are notes in Takuya’s\Nsongbook that say,
Dialogue: 0,1:46:29.21,1:46:34.01,Default,,0,0,0,,"There was a wind chime that a certain woman\Nhad that had inscribed on the inside,
Dialogue: 0,1:46:34.26,1:46:40.56,Default,,0,0,0,,"{\i1}Fuyuko, born December 17, 1913,\NJinzaburo{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:46:40.73,1:46:43.98,Default,,0,0,0,,"This moved me from the\Nvery core of my being."
Dialogue: 0,1:46:44.60,1:46:51.19,Default,,0,0,0,,Yayoi, Koyuki’s wind chime had\Njust such an inscription, didn’t it?
Dialogue: 0,1:46:52.61,1:46:57.58,Default,,0,0,0,,When I visited Mizusawa,\NI went to see Jinzaburo.
Dialogue: 0,1:46:58.24,1:47:01.12,Default,,0,0,0,,Sorry to make you come here again.
Dialogue: 0,1:47:01.33,1:47:03.54,Default,,0,0,0,,Jinzaburo is my old man.
Dialogue: 0,1:47:03.79,1:47:08.17,Default,,0,0,0,,- Was your mother a midwife?\N- Yes.
Dialogue: 0,1:47:09.55,1:47:16.43,Default,,0,0,0,,My dad always gave the mother\Na wind chime to commemorate the occasion.
Dialogue: 0,1:47:16.64,1:47:22.06,Default,,0,0,0,,They’re both long since dead,\Nso I guess you came here for nothing.
Dialogue: 0,1:47:22.31,1:47:24.64,Default,,0,0,0,,When I came before,
Dialogue: 0,1:47:24.64,1:47:27.98,Default,,0,0,0,,you said that your mother kept a record of\Nall the babies she helped to deliver.
Dialogue: 0,1:47:28.02,1:47:32.65,Default,,0,0,0,,Yeah, I found it. I had to turn the house\Nupside down to find it. It’s over there.
Dialogue: 0,1:47:32.86,1:47:33.95,Default,,0,0,0,,Thanks.
Dialogue: 0,1:47:34.11,1:47:37.53,Default,,0,0,0,,Dad bake-molded those wind chimes -\Nthey were top notch.
Dialogue: 0,1:47:37.74,1:47:40.79,Default,,0,0,0,,We were proud to inscribe\Nour name on them.
Dialogue: 0,1:47:40.83,1:47:44.96,Default,,0,0,0,,- Where is it? - Where's what?\N- The record book. - There.
Dialogue: 0,1:47:52.80,1:47:55.05,Default,,0,0,0,,From 1910.
Dialogue: 0,1:47:56.80,1:48:01.31,Default,,0,0,0,,Dad never ever sand-molded\Nthe wind chimes.
Dialogue: 0,1:48:02.89,1:48:08.73,Default,,0,0,0,,It always bugged the merchants because\Nthey couldn’t be mass-produced.
Dialogue: 0,1:48:12.15,1:48:15.36,Default,,0,0,0,,What’s wrong?
Dialogue: 0,1:48:18.11,1:48:26.00,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Fuyuko, born December 17, 1913\Nto Yayoi{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:48:27.67,1:48:31.13,Default,,0,0,0,,I immediately gave the child up\Nfor adoption.
Dialogue: 0,1:48:34.71,1:48:37.30,Default,,0,0,0,,That was the end of it.
Dialogue: 0,1:48:38.80,1:48:43.64,Default,,0,0,0,,I understand that it was the\Nadoptive parents who named her Fuyuko.
Dialogue: 0,1:48:43.68,1:48:46.73,Default,,0,0,0,,You had no idea.
Dialogue: 0,1:48:48.90,1:48:54.28,Default,,0,0,0,,Yayoi, the daughter of\Nthe midwife told me...
Dialogue: 0,1:48:55.11,1:48:58.24,Default,,0,0,0,,that a woman with a wind chime...
Dialogue: 0,1:48:58.45,1:49:01.24,Default,,0,0,0,,visited the foundry five years ago.
Dialogue: 0,1:49:01.32,1:49:03.33,Default,,0,0,0,,She had a mole on the right side\Nof her chin.
Dialogue: 0,1:49:03.41,1:49:07.00,Default,,0,0,0,,What? Five years ago?
Dialogue: 0,1:49:07.75,1:49:11.58,Default,,0,0,0,,My mother’s sick,\Nyou can’t see her.
Dialogue: 0,1:49:11.58,1:49:15.13,Default,,0,0,0,,- What do you need?\N- I'm sorry for the trouble.
Dialogue: 0,1:49:15.30,1:49:20.18,Default,,0,0,0,,My home was bombed out\Nand I had to move to another town.
Dialogue: 0,1:49:20.26,1:49:22.39,Default,,0,0,0,,That’s why I came back here.
Dialogue: 0,1:49:22.47,1:49:25.85,Default,,0,0,0,,I came because I was wondering\Nabout the wind chime.
Dialogue: 0,1:49:25.89,1:49:28.81,Default,,0,0,0,,Here’s your wind chime.
Dialogue: 0,1:49:29.02,1:49:35.19,Default,,0,0,0,,- Fuyuko, I think your mother’s\Nname is Yayoi. - What?!
Dialogue: 0,1:49:43.98,1:49:45.99,Default,,0,0,0,,Five years ago...
Dialogue: 0,1:49:46.24,1:49:49.70,Default,,0,0,0,,That’s when she came here.
Dialogue: 0,1:49:51.53,1:49:54.58,Default,,0,0,0,,To apologize, I imagine.
Dialogue: 0,1:50:01.17,1:50:04.21,Default,,0,0,0,,It has to be a coincidence that...
Dialogue: 0,1:50:04.42,1:50:09.93,Default,,0,0,0,,She learned she was sleeping with\Nher own father-in-law.
Dialogue: 0,1:50:11.97,1:50:14.18,Default,,0,0,0,,Fuyuko...
Dialogue: 0,1:50:14.35,1:50:19.77,Default,,0,0,0,,Forgive me.\NForgive me!
Dialogue: 0,1:50:38.45,1:50:42.92,Default,,0,0,0,,- Koyuki.\N- You… you’re my grandmother!
Dialogue: 0,1:50:47.88,1:50:51.43,Default,,0,0,0,,Yayoi, if I…
Dialogue: 0,1:50:54.39,1:50:58.47,Default,,0,0,0,,had been quicker….
Dialogue: 0,1:50:58.68,1:51:00.56,Default,,0,0,0,,Mr. Kindaichi.
Dialogue: 0,1:51:02.19,1:51:06.11,Default,,0,0,0,,I already knew.
Dialogue: 0,1:51:07.65,1:51:10.90,Default,,0,0,0,,I’m Yukari’s mother.
Dialogue: 0,1:51:11.74,1:51:17.66,Default,,0,0,0,,I grieved when I lost her.
Dialogue: 0,1:51:19.79,1:51:25.75,Default,,0,0,0,,But then I met Koyuki that night.
Dialogue: 0,1:51:26.00,1:51:29.17,Default,,0,0,0,,She told me,
Dialogue: 0,1:51:29.38,1:51:33.51,Default,,0,0,0,,and I knew exactly what to do.
Dialogue: 0,1:51:44.77,1:51:49.65,Default,,0,0,0,,We never guessed that Koyuki\Nwas passing for Yukari.
Dialogue: 0,1:51:49.86,1:51:54.82,Default,,0,0,0,,That’s why Yoshizawa was\Nblackmailing Shigeru.
Dialogue: 0,1:51:55.36,1:52:00.20,Default,,0,0,0,,And that’s when Shigeru found out\Nwho Koyuki was.
Dialogue: 0,1:52:00.54,1:52:04.42,Default,,0,0,0,,Shigeru in turn blackmailed Yayoi.
Dialogue: 0,1:52:04.42,1:52:07.96,Default,,0,0,0,,Shigeru never said any such thing\Nin interrogation! Did he?
Dialogue: 0,1:52:08.17,1:52:11.55,Default,,0,0,0,,I was dumbfounded when\NMokutaro told me that...
Dialogue: 0,1:52:11.76,1:52:15.55,Default,,0,0,0,,the person who summoned Yoshizawa\Non the phone had a woman’s voice.
Dialogue: 0,1:52:15.80,1:52:19.43,Default,,0,0,0,,It was Yayoi.
Dialogue: 0,1:52:19.47,1:52:24.52,Default,,0,0,0,,What?!\NThen Yayoi…!?
Dialogue: 0,1:52:33.28,1:52:36.66,Default,,0,0,0,,I made the call just as you asked,\NYayoi.
Dialogue: 0,1:52:36.86,1:52:40.20,Default,,0,0,0,,Shigeru said he’d come here.
Dialogue: 0,1:52:40.41,1:52:42.62,Default,,0,0,0,,You didn’t mention my name,\Ndid you?
Dialogue: 0,1:52:42.66,1:52:46.08,Default,,0,0,0,,Of course not.\NBut I must say,
Dialogue: 0,1:52:46.37,1:52:50.63,Default,,0,0,0,,I didn’t expect a call from you\Nabout this.
Dialogue: 0,1:52:51.67,1:52:56.05,Default,,0,0,0,,If you’re willing to meet my demands,
Dialogue: 0,1:52:56.26,1:52:59.64,Default,,0,0,0,,I don’t really care whether\NShigeru's involved.
Dialogue: 0,1:52:59.85,1:53:01.81,Default,,0,0,0,,As for me…
Dialogue: 0,1:53:33.46,1:53:36.97,Default,,0,0,0,,And Shigeru showed up after that.
Dialogue: 0,1:53:37.22,1:53:39.30,Default,,0,0,0,,Then what about Tokubei?
Dialogue: 0,1:53:39.47,1:53:42.72,Default,,0,0,0,,- He was blackmailing Yayoi.\N- Blackmail?
Dialogue: 0,1:53:42.93,1:53:45.85,Default,,0,0,0,,- Tokubei knew Yayoi’s secret.\N- What secret?
Dialogue: 0,1:53:45.93,1:53:52.94,Default,,0,0,0,,The photograph... on this dry plate.
Dialogue: 0,1:53:53.65,1:53:57.78,Default,,0,0,0,,- What photograph?\N- I can’t say.
Dialogue: 0,1:53:58.91,1:54:05.83,Default,,0,0,0,,But, as a woman, I’d think that Yayoi\Nwouldn’t ever want anyone to see it.
Dialogue: 0,1:54:06.04,1:54:10.04,Default,,0,0,0,,Tokubei’s father took the photo and kept it\Nat the Honjo Photography Studio.
Dialogue: 0,1:54:10.04,1:54:14.21,Default,,0,0,0,,- Where was the dry plate?\N- In the dark room.
Dialogue: 0,1:54:14.25,1:54:18.51,Default,,0,0,0,,- Why there? - The best hiding place\Nis out in the open.
Dialogue: 0,1:54:20.05,1:54:24.18,Default,,0,0,0,,When did he start to blackmail you?
Dialogue: 0,1:54:24.68,1:54:26.43,Default,,0,0,0,,Soon after the war.
Dialogue: 0,1:54:26.47,1:54:31.19,Default,,0,0,0,,Yayoi, if you have the dry plate\Nof a photograph,
Dialogue: 0,1:54:31.40,1:54:35.78,Default,,0,0,0,,you can make as many copies\Nas you want.
Dialogue: 0,1:54:35.82,1:54:41.49,Default,,0,0,0,,Tokubei wanted to renovate his\Noutdated photography studio.
Dialogue: 0,1:54:41.57,1:54:45.74,Default,,0,0,0,,So the wind chime in the empty building\Nthat fell on Naokichi was Yayoi, too?
Dialogue: 0,1:54:46.74,1:54:52.79,Default,,0,0,0,,It was presumably her response to\NTokubei’s exorbitant price.
Dialogue: 0,1:54:53.17,1:54:56.25,Default,,0,0,0,,The day that Tokubei was killed in\Nthe dark room, Naokichi and I...
Dialogue: 0,1:54:56.46,1:54:59.01,Default,,0,0,0,,were lured outside by a phone call\Nfrom a young man.
Dialogue: 0,1:54:59.05,1:55:02.05,Default,,0,0,0,,It was probably her rickshaw driver,\NSannosuke.
Dialogue: 0,1:55:02.26,1:55:04.51,Default,,0,0,0,,No, he had nothing to do\Nwith any of this.
Dialogue: 0,1:55:22.07,1:55:24.74,Default,,0,0,0,,Naokichi would have inherited the studio\Nwhen Tokubei died,
Dialogue: 0,1:55:24.95,1:55:27.54,Default,,0,0,0,,so he could have been trying\Nto fleece Yayoi.
Dialogue: 0,1:55:27.79,1:55:30.46,Default,,0,0,0,,He was organizing the dry plates,
Dialogue: 0,1:55:30.66,1:55:33.17,Default,,0,0,0,,so he must have known about\Nthe secret one.
Dialogue: 0,1:55:33.42,1:55:36.96,Default,,0,0,0,,I see. So Yayoi invited Naokichi to...
Dialogue: 0,1:55:37.17,1:55:40.80,Default,,0,0,0,,the House of Hanging to put the matter\Nto rest once and for all.
Dialogue: 0,1:55:40.84,1:55:45.09,Default,,0,0,0,,They say that once you’ve been blackmailed,\Nyou never forget the feeling.
Dialogue: 0,1:55:45.26,1:55:47.60,Default,,0,0,0,,Money’s the only thing that matters.
Dialogue: 0,1:55:48.01,1:55:50.18,Default,,0,0,0,,In every crime.
Dialogue: 0,1:55:50.60,1:55:54.77,Default,,0,0,0,,So what do those murders have\Nto do with the severed head?
Dialogue: 0,1:55:54.90,1:55:58.48,Default,,0,0,0,,That wasn’t a murder.
Dialogue: 0,1:55:59.36,1:56:03.53,Default,,0,0,0,,Yayoi could easily tell you\Nthe details of the case.
Dialogue: 0,1:56:03.61,1:56:07.12,Default,,0,0,0,,Enough already!\NAre you saying she did this one, too?
Dialogue: 0,1:56:07.33,1:56:11.37,Default,,0,0,0,,Look, she showed up after we'd already\Ninvestigated the murder scene.
Dialogue: 0,1:56:11.62,1:56:19.59,Default,,0,0,0,,She went into the Western-style room\Nwithout telling anyone.
Dialogue: 0,1:56:24.97,1:56:30.72,Default,,0,0,0,,You were already watching Yayoi?
Dialogue: 0,1:56:30.93,1:56:33.89,Default,,0,0,0,,Toshio’s head was...
Dialogue: 0,1:56:34.10,1:56:39.65,Default,,0,0,0,,strung up like a wind chime by\NYayoi and Koyuki.
Dialogue: 0,1:56:42.36,1:56:48.62,Default,,0,0,0,,Toshio’s wishes as written in Koyuki’s\Nsuicide note were accurate.
Dialogue: 0,1:56:48.99,1:56:54.58,Default,,0,0,0,,However, Koyuki did not kill Toshio.
Dialogue: 0,1:56:54.96,1:57:00.63,Default,,0,0,0,,I asked Koyuki to write the note.
Dialogue: 0,1:57:02.26,1:57:06.93,Default,,0,0,0,,That way, she could live as Yukari.
Dialogue: 0,1:57:07.18,1:57:10.39,Default,,0,0,0,,So what happened to Yukari?
Dialogue: 0,1:57:12.47,1:57:14.39,Default,,0,0,0,,She died.
Dialogue: 0,1:57:16.35,1:57:19.65,Default,,0,0,0,,Then, who killed Toshio?
Dialogue: 0,1:57:22.28,1:57:27.57,Default,,0,0,0,,Koyuki... please explain.
Dialogue: 0,1:57:32.74,1:57:34.37,Default,,0,0,0,,My brother, Toshio.
Dialogue: 0,1:57:47.22,1:57:49.14,Default,,0,0,0,,Do you mind the rain?
Dialogue: 0,1:57:57.77,1:57:59.98,Default,,0,0,0,,No, someone will see us.
Dialogue: 0,1:58:00.15,1:58:01.65,Default,,0,0,0,,Don’t worry.
Dialogue: 0,1:58:02.40,1:58:04.36,Default,,0,0,0,,Stop.
Dialogue: 0,1:58:41.15,1:58:46.40,Default,,0,0,0,,Hey, I hear you and Toshio used to\Nlive in the next town we’re playing in.
Dialogue: 0,1:58:46.61,1:58:48.36,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes.
Dialogue: 0,1:58:48.69,1:58:51.91,Default,,0,0,0,,I was thinking about quitting the band.
Dialogue: 0,1:58:52.03,1:58:53.49,Default,,0,0,0,,Why?
Dialogue: 0,1:58:53.95,1:58:56.83,Default,,0,0,0,,No matter what job I do,\NI want to provide for you.
Dialogue: 0,1:58:58.29,1:59:01.71,Default,,0,0,0,,I want you to come with me.
Dialogue: 0,1:59:02.83,1:59:04.34,Default,,0,0,0,,Koyuki!
Dialogue: 0,1:59:15.72,1:59:19.52,Default,,0,0,0,,- What? - What were you talking\Nto Sagawa about?
Dialogue: 0,1:59:20.35,1:59:23.56,Default,,0,0,0,,- Nothing.\N- Koyuki...
Dialogue: 0,1:59:27.48,1:59:29.40,Default,,0,0,0,,marry me.
Dialogue: 0,1:59:30.78,1:59:34.87,Default,,0,0,0,,We’ve been together since\Nwe were small,
Dialogue: 0,1:59:36.08,1:59:40.04,Default,,0,0,0,,your romance with Sagawa is\Njust a fling. I know all about it.
Dialogue: 0,1:59:40.25,1:59:43.33,Default,,0,0,0,,- Why don’t you listen?!\N- I do.
Dialogue: 0,1:59:43.33,1:59:44.83,Default,,0,0,0,,You don’t!
Dialogue: 0,1:59:45.42,1:59:51.13,Default,,0,0,0,,I told you to forget about revenge…
Dialogue: 0,1:59:51.26,1:59:54.26,Default,,0,0,0,,I don’t go back on a decision.
Dialogue: 0,1:59:54.64,1:59:58.10,Default,,0,0,0,,I'll lure Yukari out once we\Nget to town.
Dialogue: 0,2:00:01.27,2:00:03.52,Default,,0,0,0,,I don’t want to go back there.
Dialogue: 0,2:00:03.73,2:00:09.11,Default,,0,0,0,,Everything I’m doing is for you.
Dialogue: 0,2:00:09.36,2:00:12.65,Default,,0,0,0,,- No, it isn’t!\N- I'm serious! Marry me! - No!
Dialogue: 0,2:00:20.75,2:00:23.04,Default,,0,0,0,,You don’t love me, Toshio.
Dialogue: 0,2:00:25.54,2:00:27.84,Default,,0,0,0,,I need you to love me.
Dialogue: 0,2:00:27.88,2:00:33.17,Default,,0,0,0,,Let me out!\NI'll scream!
Dialogue: 0,2:00:34.38,2:00:38.47,Default,,0,0,0,,We’re far from town.\NGive it up.
Dialogue: 0,2:00:39.64,2:00:43.27,Default,,0,0,0,,I came because you said you wanted me\Nto meet my sister!
Dialogue: 0,2:00:43.56,2:00:45.19,Default,,0,0,0,,You lied!
Dialogue: 0,2:00:47.02,2:00:52.78,Default,,0,0,0,,Not that I considered the daughter of\Nmy father's mistress any kind of a sister!
Dialogue: 0,2:00:53.03,2:00:54.11,Default,,0,0,0,,Shaddap!
Dialogue: 0,2:00:57.41,2:00:59.49,Default,,0,0,0,,What do you want from me?
Dialogue: 0,2:01:01.74,2:01:03.96,Default,,0,0,0,,My mother will pay anything you ask!
Dialogue: 0,2:01:04.21,2:01:07.96,Default,,0,0,0,,Please!
Dialogue: 0,2:01:12.34,2:01:16.09,Default,,0,0,0,,Help! Help!
Dialogue: 0,2:01:19.01,2:01:20.60,Default,,0,0,0,,It’s your little sister.
Dialogue: 0,2:01:21.14,2:01:25.85,Default,,0,0,0,,Did you know from the start that you look\Nnearly identical to your sister?
Dialogue: 0,2:01:26.06,2:01:32.90,Default,,0,0,0,,No. I’m sure you were surprised\Nby the resemblance.
Dialogue: 0,2:01:41.74,2:01:44.58,Default,,0,0,0,,- It's you.\N- You give me the creeps.
Dialogue: 0,2:01:44.87,2:01:50.08,Default,,0,0,0,,A surprise, no? When I first met her,\NI thought she was you.
Dialogue: 0,2:01:55.84,2:01:59.26,Default,,0,0,0,,- Toshio, let her go.\N- It’s too late for that.
Dialogue: 0,2:01:59.47,2:02:01.80,Default,,0,0,0,,Our mother wouldn’t have wanted this.
Dialogue: 0,2:02:02.72,2:02:06.10,Default,,0,0,0,,It was as if the Hogens had murdered her\Nwith their own hands.
Dialogue: 0,2:02:07.06,2:02:09.15,Default,,0,0,0,,We made a pact in front of\Nour mother’s dangling corpse!
Dialogue: 0,2:02:09.23,2:02:13.48,Default,,0,0,0,,What do I have to do with the woman\Nwho hanged herself in the House?
Dialogue: 0,2:02:14.36,2:02:20.82,Default,,0,0,0,,I didn’t want to meet you like this.
Dialogue: 0,2:02:20.95,2:02:23.87,Default,,0,0,0,,Koyuki!\NGo upstairs.
Dialogue: 0,2:02:23.91,2:02:27.83,Default,,0,0,0,,Yeah, I wouldn’t want you\Nto rescue me anyhow.
Dialogue: 0,2:02:28.08,2:02:31.83,Default,,0,0,0,,The girl of a family that disgraced\Nmy father’s good name.
Dialogue: 0,2:03:23.05,2:03:28.39,Default,,0,0,0,,Hey, is the photographer here?
Dialogue: 0,2:03:28.47,2:03:30.14,Default,,0,0,0,,I asked him to come.
Dialogue: 0,2:03:31.19,2:03:33.44,Default,,0,0,0,,Throw away the syringe.
Dialogue: 0,2:03:35.48,2:03:38.44,Default,,0,0,0,,- Was anyone out front?\N- No.
Dialogue: 0,2:03:41.20,2:03:43.57,Default,,0,0,0,,Don’t forget to hang the wind chimes.
Dialogue: 0,2:03:52.50,2:03:55.17,Default,,0,0,0,,He said they’d have the photos\Nready in three days.
Dialogue: 0,2:04:29.33,2:04:32.46,Default,,0,0,0,,We’re going to take Yukari home\Nonce the drugs wear off, right?
Dialogue: 0,2:04:32.66,2:04:34.04,Default,,0,0,0,,Sure.
Dialogue: 0,2:04:34.25,2:04:36.92,Default,,0,0,0,,We need to change her clothes.
Dialogue: 0,2:04:37.63,2:04:41.01,Default,,0,0,0,,- I'll get them.\N- Koyuki!
Dialogue: 0,2:04:41.26,2:04:46.64,Default,,0,0,0,,- Are you going to marry Sagawa?\N- I...
Dialogue: 0,2:04:47.80,2:04:52.64,Default,,0,0,0,,I’m going to stay with you\Nuntil you get married.
Dialogue: 0,2:05:12.04,2:05:14.12,Default,,0,0,0,,- Hey!\N- Stay away!
Dialogue: 0,2:05:15.92,2:05:19.96,Default,,0,0,0,,Why am I dressed up like this?!\NWhat did you do to me?!
Dialogue: 0,2:05:20.17,2:05:22.30,Default,,0,0,0,,- I took your photo.\N- My photo?
Dialogue: 0,2:05:22.51,2:05:24.38,Default,,0,0,0,,I plan to send it to your house.
Dialogue: 0,2:05:24.59,2:05:27.14,Default,,0,0,0,,You’re going to blackmail me!
Dialogue: 0,2:05:27.34,2:05:29.97,Default,,0,0,0,,It’s not blackmail...
Dialogue: 0,2:05:31.01,2:05:33.39,Default,,0,0,0,,- it’s revenge.\N- You bastard!
Dialogue: 0,2:05:33.60,2:05:35.69,Default,,0,0,0,,I'll call the police!
Dialogue: 0,2:05:38.35,2:05:42.53,Default,,0,0,0,,- You’re not going anywhere.\N- I’m going home.
Dialogue: 0,2:05:59.71,2:06:01.42,Default,,0,0,0,,Koyuki!
Dialogue: 0,2:06:07.09,2:06:08.93,Default,,0,0,0,,She died.
Dialogue: 0,2:06:14.85,2:06:17.48,Default,,0,0,0,,I killed her.
Dialogue: 0,2:06:21.98,2:06:25.99,Default,,0,0,0,,Yukari... Yukari!
Dialogue: 0,2:07:00.44,2:07:03.06,Default,,0,0,0,,Toshio!
Dialogue: 0,2:07:06.07,2:07:12.82,Default,,0,0,0,,Koyuki... do me a favor...
Dialogue: 0,2:07:13.03,2:07:14.87,Default,,0,0,0,,Don’t go!
Dialogue: 0,2:07:15.08,2:07:17.58,Default,,0,0,0,,Cut off my head.
Dialogue: 0,2:07:17.79,2:07:23.67,Default,,0,0,0,,And hang it in the House of Hanging.
Dialogue: 0,2:07:24.79,2:07:28.13,Default,,0,0,0,,Hang Dad’s song on it.
Dialogue: 0,2:07:28.97,2:07:33.55,Default,,0,0,0,,Send the photo to the Hogens.
Dialogue: 0,2:07:33.76,2:07:37.77,Default,,0,0,0,,Do you know what you’re saying?!
Dialogue: 0,2:07:39.60,2:07:42.90,Default,,0,0,0,,I want them to know how I feel.
Dialogue: 0,2:07:45.02,2:07:48.78,Default,,0,0,0,,And how our dearly departed\Nmother felt.
Dialogue: 0,2:07:52.16,2:07:57.49,Default,,0,0,0,,It’s the last thing I can do for you.
Dialogue: 0,2:08:00.04,2:08:02.62,Default,,0,0,0,,Toshio!
Dialogue: 0,2:08:09.84,2:08:14.09,Default,,0,0,0,,Why did you telephone the Hogens?
Dialogue: 0,2:08:16.39,2:08:20.10,Default,,0,0,0,,She couldn’t have done it herself.
Dialogue: 0,2:08:22.14,2:08:26.44,Default,,0,0,0,,Someone helped her...
Dialogue: 0,2:08:27.36,2:08:32.32,Default,,0,0,0,,Someone aside from Yayoi.
Dialogue: 0,2:08:35.41,2:08:42.58,Default,,0,0,0,,Koyuki telephoned after 10:00pm.
Dialogue: 0,2:08:42.66,2:08:47.08,Default,,0,0,0,,What?! What about Yukari?!
Dialogue: 0,2:08:52.26,2:08:59.97,Default,,0,0,0,,I only found out that she’d died\Nthree days after it happened.
Dialogue: 0,2:09:02.98,2:09:09.02,Default,,0,0,0,,I couldn’t even process\Nwhat Koyuki had said.
Dialogue: 0,2:09:09.23,2:09:14.32,Default,,0,0,0,,You’re a Hogen, why did you share\NToshio’s thirst for revenge?
Dialogue: 0,2:09:14.49,2:09:20.99,Default,,0,0,0,,Because Koyuki and Yayoi...
Dialogue: 0,2:09:21.20,2:09:23.79,Default,,0,0,0,,have a lot in common.
Dialogue: 0,2:09:26.04,2:09:29.13,Default,,0,0,0,,I felt bad for Koyuki.
Dialogue: 0,2:09:31.25,2:09:37.26,Default,,0,0,0,,I asked her to come in the back door,\Nso no one would notice.
Dialogue: 0,2:09:39.68,2:09:45.48,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}That was the first time\NI ever met Koyuki.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,2:09:49.23,2:09:51.90,Default,,0,0,0,,You’re not Yukari?
Dialogue: 0,2:09:53.61,2:09:58.36,Default,,0,0,0,,What are you doing?\NQuit fooling around.
Dialogue: 0,2:09:58.57,2:10:00.24,Default,,0,0,0,,No...
Dialogue: 0,2:10:00.58,2:10:05.08,Default,,0,0,0,,I’m Koyuki Yamauchi.
Dialogue: 0,2:10:07.79,2:10:13.05,Default,,0,0,0,,Help me;\Nmy brother had a dying wish.
Dialogue: 0,2:10:13.25,2:10:16.13,Default,,0,0,0,,I don’t care what happens to me.
Dialogue: 0,2:10:16.30,2:10:19.47,Default,,0,0,0,,Please!
Dialogue: 0,2:10:21.22,2:10:23.26,Default,,0,0,0,,Please!
Dialogue: 0,2:11:46.06,2:11:48.32,Default,,0,0,0,,Koyuki...
Dialogue: 0,2:11:51.03,2:11:59.12,Default,,0,0,0,,You must have felt like you were\Nwalking on egg shells for years.
Dialogue: 0,2:12:02.79,2:12:10.55,Default,,0,0,0,,And how horrible the last few days\Nhave been for you.
Dialogue: 0,2:12:10.80,2:12:14.17,Default,,0,0,0,,I don't blame you, Mom.
Dialogue: 0,2:12:16.59,2:12:20.43,Default,,0,0,0,,I’m Yukari.
Dialogue: 0,2:12:22.56,2:12:24.60,Default,,0,0,0,,Yukari.
Dialogue: 0,2:12:27.44,2:12:29.82,Default,,0,0,0,,Thank you.
Dialogue: 0,2:12:34.40,2:12:39.03,Default,,0,0,0,,Where did you dump\NYukari’s and Toshio’s bodies?
Dialogue: 0,2:12:39.28,2:12:43.70,Default,,0,0,0,,Yukari liked the ocean.
Dialogue: 0,2:12:44.46,2:12:50.67,Default,,0,0,0,,I buried them by the sea\Nin Matsubara City.
Dialogue: 0,2:12:55.17,2:12:58.43,Default,,0,0,0,,The mistress has died.
Dialogue: 0,2:13:00.39,2:13:03.06,Default,,0,0,0,,Who else is there involved?!
Dialogue: 0,2:13:07.48,2:13:09.56,Default,,0,0,0,,Where are you going?!
Dialogue: 0,2:13:11.82,2:13:13.44,Default,,0,0,0,,It’s here!
Dialogue: 0,2:13:34.21,2:13:40.59,Default,,0,0,0,,Koyuki... this is Yayoi’s mother.
Dialogue: 0,2:13:40.80,2:13:44.06,Default,,0,0,0,,She’s been bedridden for a long time.
Dialogue: 0,2:13:46.73,2:13:50.56,Default,,0,0,0,,Was she here alone?
Dialogue: 0,2:13:50.73,2:13:55.90,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes... Everyone’s alone.
Dialogue: 0,2:13:56.11,2:13:59.03,Default,,0,0,0,,- Where’s Yayoi?\N- What?
Dialogue: 0,2:13:59.74,2:14:02.12,Default,,0,0,0,,Not on my watch!
Dialogue: 0,2:14:08.50,2:14:10.33,Default,,0,0,0,,She’s gone!
Dialogue: 0,2:14:11.46,2:14:15.25,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, fudge!\NFind her!
Dialogue: 0,2:14:19.63,2:14:21.89,Default,,0,0,0,,Mom!
Dialogue: 0,2:14:30.81,2:14:34.27,Default,,0,0,0,,- I know she’s…\N- Koyuki!
Dialogue: 0,2:14:36.73,2:14:39.03,Default,,0,0,0,,Let the police find her.
Dialogue: 0,2:14:41.95,2:14:44.95,Default,,0,0,0,,I was sure she came with us!
Dialogue: 0,2:14:45.12,2:14:47.70,Default,,0,0,0,,You were too busy scratching\Nyour behind to notice!
Dialogue: 0,2:14:47.91,2:14:51.04,Default,,0,0,0,,Sir, the dry plate is crucial\Nphysical evidence.
Dialogue: 0,2:14:52.88,2:14:55.79,Default,,0,0,0,,I don’t know anything about\Nany dry plate.
Dialogue: 0,2:15:29.50,2:15:33.62,Default,,0,0,0,,Sannosuke...
Dialogue: 0,2:15:33.79,2:15:37.46,Default,,0,0,0,,what would I have done without you?
Dialogue: 0,2:15:37.88,2:15:39.92,Default,,0,0,0,,It was nothing, madam.
Dialogue: 0,2:15:40.09,2:15:46.80,Default,,0,0,0,,The empty building,\Nthe phone calls you made for me...
Dialogue: 0,2:15:47.01,2:15:53.02,Default,,0,0,0,,You buried Yukari and Toshio for me.
Dialogue: 0,2:15:53.19,2:15:56.86,Default,,0,0,0,,What will become of the house of Hogen?
Dialogue: 0,2:15:57.40,2:16:01.28,Default,,0,0,0,,Koyuki can manage.
Dialogue: 0,2:16:04.49,2:16:09.83,Default,,0,0,0,,We’re almost at the Hogen Hospital.
Dialogue: 0,2:16:11.91,2:16:16.33,Default,,0,0,0,,Fuyuko is waiting.
Dialogue: 0,2:16:21.71,2:16:24.76,Default,,0,0,0,,Madam, we’re here.
Dialogue: 0,2:17:47.84,2:17:51.64,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm starting to wonder whether Mr. Kindaichi\Neven plans to come back from the US.
Dialogue: 0,2:17:51.89,2:17:56.39,Default,,0,0,0,,He sent us a letter from San Francisco\Nabout three months ago.
Dialogue: 0,2:17:57.43,2:17:59.60,Default,,0,0,0,,He’s kind of a pessimist.
Dialogue: 0,2:17:59.77,2:18:03.27,Default,,0,0,0,,I think it’s just an act.
Dialogue: 0,2:18:03.44,2:18:06.36,Default,,0,0,0,,I think he’s actually an optimist.
Dialogue: 0,2:18:08.57,2:18:14.91,Default,,0,0,0,,By the way, do you have\Nany work for me? I'll do anything.
Dialogue: 0,2:18:15.12,2:18:16.79,Default,,0,0,0,,I thought you had a job at\Nthe photography studio.
Dialogue: 0,2:18:17.00,2:18:19.83,Default,,0,0,0,,It was shuttered as soon as I quit.
Dialogue: 0,2:18:21.00,2:18:23.59,Default,,0,0,0,,I wonder what will happen to\Nthe Hogen family?
Dialogue: 0,2:18:23.79,2:18:26.30,Default,,0,0,0,,Old things pass.
Dialogue: 0,2:18:26.55,2:18:30.01,Default,,0,0,0,,That’s when new things are born.
Dialogue: 0,2:18:34.81,2:18:37.81,Default,,0,0,0,,- Hello.\N- Pleased to meet you.
Dialogue: 0,2:18:38.02,2:18:39.81,Default,,0,0,0,,English breakfast tea again?
Dialogue: 0,2:18:41.31,2:18:52.20,Default,,0,0,0,,
